/-!
# Flips and finite generation of divisorial algebras

This file proves Kollár–Mori's criterion for the existence of flips, together with the graded
algebra it rests on.

*Veronese subalgebras.* Let `A` be a Noetherian ring and `R = ⨁_{m ≥ 0} R_m` a graded
`A`-algebra which is a domain. For `d ≥ 1`, `R` is of finite type over `A` if and only if its
Veronese subalgebra `R^(d) = ⨁_m R_{dm}` is. The same holds for a quasi-coherent graded algebra
`R` over a Noetherian scheme `Y` whose rings of sections over nonempty affine opens are domains,
and if `R` is of finite type and `Y` is quasi-compact, some `R^(d)` is generated by `R_0` and
`R_d`: a product of generators of total degree at least `m * m!`, all of degree at most `m`,
contains `m! / e` factors of a single degree `e`.

*Small ample models.* Let `Y` be a normal variety and `B` a Weil divisor on `Y`. The divisorial
algebra `R(Y, B) = ⨁_{m ≥ 0} 𝒪_Y(mB)` is a sheaf of finitely generated `𝒪_Y`-algebras if and
only if there is a small projective birational `g : Z ⟶ Y` from a normal variety on which the
birational transform `g⁻¹_* B` is `ℚ`-Cartier and `g`-ample: one takes `Z = Proj_Y R(Y, dB)`
with `R(Y, dB)` generated in degree one, and conversely `R(Y, B)(U) ≅ ⨁_m 𝒪_Z(m g⁻¹_* B)(g⁻¹U)`.
Applied to `B = f_*(rK + rD)`, this says that the flip of a `(K + D)`-flipping contraction `f`
exists if and only if `R(Y, f_*(rK + rD))` is finitely generated.

*A divisor on a common model.* Given proper normal varieties `X₁`, `X₂` over `S` and a
birational map between them, the common normal model `Z` can be chosen so that a given divisor
`E` over `X₁` is a prime divisor of `Z`: the valuation ring of `E` is realised as a local ring
by blowing up a model of its centre and normalizing.

## Main results

* `MMP.Fourfold.finiteType_iff_veroneseSubalgebra_fg`: a graded domain over a Noetherian ring is
  of finite type iff its `d`-th Veronese subalgebra is.
* `MMP.Fourfold.isFiniteTypeOverBase_iff_veronese_fg`: the same for a graded sheaf of domains.
* `MMP.Fourfold.exists_veronese_eq_adjoin_degree`: some Veronese subalgebra of a graded sheaf of
  finite type is generated in degrees `0` and `d`.
* `MMP.Mori.Divisor.exists_isSmallAmpleModel_of_finiteType_divisorialAlgebra`: a finitely
  generated divisorial algebra has a small ample model (KM 6.2, (1) ⇒ (2)).
* `MMP.Mori.Divisor.finiteType_divisorialAlgebraSections_of_inverseTransformDivisor`: a small
  ample model makes the divisorial algebra finitely generated (KM 6.2, (2) ⇒ (1)).
* `MMP.Mori.Divisor.finiteType_divisorialAlgebraSections_of_isRelativelyFreeDivisor`: the same
  with a Cartier `g`-free multiple of `g⁻¹_* B` in place of a `g`-ample one.
* `MMP.Mori.exists_isFlip_iff_finiteType_divisorialAlgebraSections`: a flip exists iff the
  divisorial algebra of `f_*(rK + rD)` is finitely generated (KM 6.4(2)).
* `MMP.Mori.exists_isNormalVariety_isProper_isBirationalMorphism_primeDivisor_valuation_eq`:
  the common normal model on which a given divisor over `X₁` is a prime divisor.

## Implementation notes

A graded quasi-coherent `𝒪_Y`-algebra is a `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation`, and "a sheaf of
finitely generated `𝒪_Y`-algebras" is stated over every affine open `U`: the ring of sections
`R(U)` is of finite type over `Γ(Y, U)`. The Veronese subalgebra of a graded sheaf is stated
through its rings of sections: the sections of `R(U)` whose homogeneous components in degrees
not divisible by `d` vanish. Its generation in degree one is stated with `R_0(U) ∪ R_d(U)` as
generators, since `R_0` need not be the image of `𝒪_Y`.

That `g⁻¹_* B` is `ℚ`-Cartier and `g`-ample is `MMP.Mori.QDivisor.HasRelativelyAmpleMultiple`
of the associated `ℚ`-divisor. The integral divisor `rD` of the flip criterion is a `ℤ`-divisor
`Dr` with `Dr = r • D` as `ℚ`-divisors.

That the centre of `E` on `Z` is a prime divisor with the valuation of `E` is stated as the
existence of a prime divisor `P` of `Z` such that the divisor `(Z, g₁, P)` over `X₁` has the
valuation of `E`; on the separated scheme `Z` this pins `P` as the centre.

## References

* [J. Kollár, S. Mori, *Birational geometry of algebraic varieties*][KollarMori1998], 2.45, the
  proofs of 3.38 and 3.51, Lemma 6.2 and Corollary 6.4.
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory

universe u

namespace MMP.Fourfold

/-- A graded domain `R` over a Noetherian ring `A` is finitely generated over `A` if and only
if its `d`-th Veronese subalgebra `R^(d)` is, for every `d ≥ 1`. -/
@[mmp "lem_fourfold_veronese_fg"]
public theorem finiteType_iff_veroneseSubalgebra_fg {A R : Type*} [CommRing A]
    [IsNoetherianRing A] [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [Algebra A R]
    (𝒜 : ℕ → Submodule A R) [GradedAlgebra 𝒜] {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d) :
    Algebra.FiniteType A R ↔ (veroneseSubalgebra 𝒜 d).FG := by
  refine ⟨fun _ => veroneseSubalgebra_fg 𝒜 hd, fun h => ?_⟩
  have := (Subalgebra.fg_iff_finiteType _).mp h
  have := Algebra.FiniteType.isNoetherianRing A (veroneseSubalgebra 𝒜 d)
  have := module_finite_veroneseSubalgebra 𝒜 hd
  exact .trans (S := veroneseSubalgebra 𝒜 d) inferInstance inferInstance

open DirectSum

section Algebraic

variable {A R : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing R] [Algebra A R]
  (𝒜 : ℕ → Submodule A R) [GradedAlgebra 𝒜]

private theorem mul_le_graded (i j : ℕ) : 𝒜 i * 𝒜 j ≤ 𝒜 (i + j) :=
  Submodule.mul_le.mpr fun _ hx _ hy => SetLike.mul_mem_graded hx hy

private theorem prod_map_le (D : Multiset ℕ) : (D.map 𝒜).prod ≤ 𝒜 D.sum := by
  induction D using Multiset.induction_on with
  | empty => simpa using Submodule.one_le.mpr (SetLike.GradedOne.one_mem (A := 𝒜))
  | cons a D ih =>
    rw [Multiset.map_cons, Multiset.prod_cons, Multiset.sum_cons]
    exact Submodule.mul_le.mpr fun x hx y hy => SetLike.mul_mem_graded hx (ih hy)

/-- The span of the products `R_0 ⋅ R_{e₁} ⋯ R_{e_r}` with `1 ≤ eᵢ ≤ m` and `∑ eᵢ = n`. -/
private noncomputable def gen (m n : ℕ) : Submodule A R :=
  ⨆ (D : Multiset ℕ) (_ : (∀ e ∈ D, 1 ≤ e ∧ e ≤ m) ∧ D.sum = n), 𝒜 0 * (D.map 𝒜).prod

private theorem gen_le (m n : ℕ) : gen 𝒜 m n ≤ 𝒜 n :=
  iSup₂_le fun D hD => by
    rw [← hD.2]
    exact Submodule.mul_le.mpr fun x hx y hy => by
      simpa using SetLike.mul_mem_graded hx (prod_map_le 𝒜 D hy)

private theorem gen_mul (m p q : ℕ) : gen 𝒜 m p * gen 𝒜 m q ≤ gen 𝒜 m (p + q) := by
  have h00 : 𝒜 0 * 𝒜 0 ≤ 𝒜 0 := by simpa using mul_le_graded 𝒜 0 0
  simp only [gen, Submodule.iSup_mul, Submodule.mul_iSup]
  refine iSup_le fun D => iSup_le fun hD => iSup_le fun D' => iSup_le fun hD' => ?_
  refine le_iSup₂_of_le (D + D') ⟨fun e he => ?_, by simp [hD.2, hD'.2, add_comm]⟩ ?_
  · rcases Multiset.mem_add.mp he with he | he
    exacts [hD.1 e he, hD'.1 e he]
  · rw [Multiset.map_add, Multiset.prod_add]
    first
      | (rw [mul_mul_mul_comm]; exact mul_le_mul' h00 le_rfl)
      | (rw [mul_comm (Multiset.prod (D.map 𝒜)), mul_mul_mul_comm]; exact mul_le_mul' h00 le_rfl)

private theorem le_gen {m i : ℕ} (hi : i ≤ m) : 𝒜 i ≤ gen 𝒜 m i := by
  rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos i with rfl | hi0
  · exact le_iSup₂_of_le (0 : Multiset ℕ) ⟨by simp, by simp⟩ (by simp)
  · refine le_iSup₂_of_le ({i} : Multiset ℕ) ⟨fun e he => ?_, by simp⟩ ?_
    · rw [Multiset.mem_singleton] at he
      exact he ▸ ⟨hi0, hi⟩
    intro x hx
    simpa using Submodule.mul_mem_mul (SetLike.GradedOne.one_mem (A := 𝒜)) hx

private theorem mem_of_mem_iSup {N : ℕ → Submodule A R} (hN : ∀ n, N n ≤ 𝒜 n) {n : ℕ} {x : R}
    (hx : x ∈ 𝒜 n) (hx' : x ∈ ⨆ i, N i) : x ∈ N n := by
  classical
  have key : ⨆ i, N i ≤ (N n).comap (GradedAlgebra.proj 𝒜 n) := iSup_le fun i y hy => by
    simp only [Submodule.mem_comap, GradedAlgebra.proj_apply]
    by_cases h : i = n
    · subst h; rw [DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same 𝒜 (hN i hy)]; exact hy
    · rw [DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_ne 𝒜 (hN i hy) h]; exact zero_mem _
  simpa [Submodule.mem_comap, GradedAlgebra.proj_apply, DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same 𝒜 hx]
    using key hx'

/-- The homogeneous elements of degree at most `m`. -/
private def lowDeg (m : ℕ) : Set R := {x | ∃ i ≤ m, x ∈ 𝒜 i}

private theorem mem_gen {m : ℕ} (hgen : Algebra.adjoin A (lowDeg 𝒜 m) = ⊤) {n : ℕ} {x : R}
    (hx : x ∈ 𝒜 n) : x ∈ gen 𝒜 m n := by
  refine mem_of_mem_iSup 𝒜 (gen_le 𝒜 m) hx ?_
  let B : Subalgebra A R := (⨆ n, gen 𝒜 m n).toSubalgebra
    (Submodule.mem_iSup_of_mem 0 (le_gen 𝒜 (Nat.zero_le m) (SetLike.GradedOne.one_mem)))
    (fun a b ha hb => by
      have hle : (⨆ n, gen 𝒜 m n) * (⨆ n, gen 𝒜 m n) ≤ ⨆ n, gen 𝒜 m n := by
        simp only [Submodule.iSup_mul, Submodule.mul_iSup]
        exact iSup_le fun p => iSup_le fun q => (gen_mul 𝒜 m _ _).trans (le_iSup _ _)
      exact hle (Submodule.mul_mem_mul ha hb))
  have hle : Algebra.adjoin A (lowDeg 𝒜 m) ≤ B := Algebra.adjoin_le fun y ⟨i, hi, hy⟩ =>
    Submodule.mem_iSup_of_mem i (le_gen 𝒜 hi hy)
  rw [hgen] at hle
  exact hle (Algebra.mem_top (x := x))

private theorem exists_le_count {m : ℕ} (hm : 1 ≤ m) (D : Multiset ℕ)
    (hD : ∀ e ∈ D, 1 ≤ e ∧ e ≤ m) (hs : m * m.factorial ≤ D.sum) :
    ∃ e, 1 ≤ e ∧ e ≤ m ∧ m.factorial / e ≤ D.count e := by
  classical
  by_contra h
  push Not at h
  set L := m.factorial
  have hL : 1 ≤ L := Nat.factorial_pos m
  have h1 : ∀ e ∈ D.toFinset, D.count e • e + 1 ≤ L := by
    intro e he
    obtain ⟨he1, hem⟩ := hD e (Multiset.mem_toFinset.mp he)
    have hc := h e he1 hem
    have hdiv : L / e * e = L := Nat.div_mul_cancel (Nat.dvd_factorial he1 hem)
    have : (D.count e + 1) * e ≤ L / e * e := Nat.mul_le_mul_right e hc
    rw [smul_eq_mul]
    nlinarith
  have hsum := Finset.sum_le_sum h1
  rw [Finset.sum_add_distrib, ← Finset.sum_multiset_count, Finset.sum_const, Finset.sum_const,
    smul_eq_mul, smul_eq_mul, mul_one] at hsum
  have hcard : D.toFinset.card ≤ m := by
    calc D.toFinset.card ≤ (Finset.Icc 1 m).card := Finset.card_le_card fun e he => by
          obtain ⟨a, b⟩ := hD e (Multiset.mem_toFinset.mp he); simp [a, b]
      _ = m := by simp
  have hcL : D.toFinset.card * L ≤ m * L := Nat.mul_le_mul_right L hcard
  have hmL : 1 ≤ m * L := Nat.mul_le_mul hm hL
  rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos D.toFinset.card with h0 | h0
  · rw [h0, zero_mul] at hsum; omega
  · omega

private theorem le_mul_of_le {m : ℕ} (hm : 1 ≤ m) (hgen : Algebra.adjoin A (lowDeg 𝒜 m) = ⊤)
    {n : ℕ} (hn : m * m.factorial ≤ n) :
    𝒜 n ≤ 𝒜 m.factorial * 𝒜 (n - m.factorial) := by
  classical
  intro x hx
  refine (iSup₂_le fun D hD => ?_ : gen 𝒜 m n ≤ _) (mem_gen 𝒜 hgen hx)
  obtain ⟨hD, hsum⟩ := hD
  obtain ⟨e, he1, hem, hc⟩ := exists_le_count hm D hD (hsum ▸ hn)
  set L := m.factorial
  have hrep := Multiset.le_count_iff_replicate_le.mp hc
  set D' := D - Multiset.replicate (L / e) e
  have hDD : D = Multiset.replicate (L / e) e + D' := (add_tsub_cancel_of_le hrep).symm
  have hdiv : L / e * e = L := Nat.div_mul_cancel (Nat.dvd_factorial he1 hem)
  have hs' : D'.sum = n - L := by
    have := congrArg Multiset.sum hDD
    rw [Multiset.sum_add, Multiset.sum_replicate, smul_eq_mul, hdiv] at this
    omega
  have h1 := prod_map_le 𝒜 (Multiset.replicate (L / e) e)
  rw [Multiset.sum_replicate, smul_eq_mul, hdiv] at h1
  have h2 := prod_map_le 𝒜 D'
  rw [hs'] at h2
  have h0L : 𝒜 0 * 𝒜 L ≤ 𝒜 L := by simpa using mul_le_graded 𝒜 0 L
  rw [hDD, Multiset.map_add, Multiset.prod_add, ← mul_assoc]
  exact mul_le_mul' ((mul_le_mul' le_rfl h1).trans h0L) h2

private theorem le_veronese {m : ℕ} (hm : 1 ≤ m) (hgen : Algebra.adjoin A (lowDeg 𝒜 m) = ⊤)
    (k : ℕ) : 𝒜 (m * m.factorial * k) ≤
      Subalgebra.toSubmodule (Algebra.adjoin A ((𝒜 0 : Set R) ∪ 𝒜 (m * m.factorial))) := by
  obtain ⟨L, hLdef⟩ : ∃ L, m.factorial = L := ⟨_, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨d, hddef⟩ : ∃ d, m * L = d := ⟨_, rfl⟩
  rw [hLdef, hddef]
  have hL : 1 ≤ L := hLdef ▸ Nat.factorial_pos m
  -- splitting off `m` factors of degree `L`
  have hstep : ∀ k, 1 ≤ k → ∀ j ≤ m, 𝒜 (d * k + d) ≤ 𝒜 L ^ j * 𝒜 (d * k + d - j * L) := by
    intro k hk j
    induction j with
    | zero => intro _; simp
    | succ j ih =>
      intro hj
      have hjL : j * L + L ≤ m * L := by
        simpa [add_mul] using Nat.mul_le_mul_right L hj
      have hdk : d ≤ d * k := Nat.le_mul_of_pos_right d hk
      rw [hddef] at hjL
      refine (ih (by omega)).trans ?_
      rw [pow_succ, mul_assoc (𝒜 L ^ j)]
      refine mul_le_mul' le_rfl ?_
      have := le_mul_of_le 𝒜 hm hgen (n := d * k + d - j * L) (by rw [hLdef]; omega)
      rw [hLdef] at this
      have he : d * k + d - j * L - L = d * k + d - (j + 1) * L := by rw [add_mul, one_mul]; omega
      rwa [he] at this
  have hpow : 𝒜 L ^ m ≤ 𝒜 d := by
    have := prod_map_le 𝒜 (Multiset.replicate m L)
    rw [← hddef]
    simpa [Multiset.map_replicate, Multiset.prod_replicate, Multiset.sum_replicate] using this
  have hsplit : ∀ k, 1 ≤ k → 𝒜 (d * (k + 1)) ≤ 𝒜 d * 𝒜 (d * k) := by
    intro k hk
    have := hstep k hk m le_rfl
    rw [show d * k + d - m * L = d * k by omega, ← mul_add_one] at this
    exact this.trans (mul_le_mul' hpow le_rfl)
  set B := Algebra.adjoin A ((𝒜 0 : Set R) ∪ 𝒜 d)
  clear hstep
  induction k with
  | zero =>
    intro x hx
    rw [mul_zero] at hx
    exact Algebra.subset_adjoin (Or.inl hx)
  | succ k ih =>
    rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos k with rfl | hk
    · intro x hx
      rw [zero_add, mul_one] at hx
      exact Algebra.subset_adjoin (Or.inr hx)
    · refine (hsplit k hk).trans (Submodule.mul_le.mpr fun x hx y hy => B.mul_mem ?_ (ih hy))
      exact Algebra.subset_adjoin (Or.inr hx)

private theorem exists_adjoin_lowDeg_eq_top [Algebra.FiniteType A R] :
    ∃ m, 1 ≤ m ∧ Algebra.adjoin A (lowDeg 𝒜 m) = ⊤ := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨G, hG⟩ := Algebra.FiniteType.out (R := A) (A := R)
  refine ⟨max 1 (G.sup fun g => (decompose 𝒜 g).support.sup id), le_max_left _ _, ?_⟩
  rw [eq_top_iff, ← hG]
  refine Algebra.adjoin_le fun g hg => ?_
  rw [← DirectSum.sum_support_decompose 𝒜 g]
  refine Subalgebra.sum_mem _ fun i hi => Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨i, ?_, (decompose 𝒜 g i).2⟩
  exact le_max_of_le_right ((Finset.le_sup (f := id) hi).trans
    (Finset.le_sup (f := fun g => (decompose 𝒜 g).support.sup id) hg))

private theorem lowDeg_mono {m m' : ℕ} (h : m ≤ m') : lowDeg 𝒜 m ⊆ lowDeg 𝒜 m' :=
  fun _ ⟨i, hi, hx⟩ => ⟨i, hi.trans h, hx⟩

end Algebraic

section GradedHom

variable {A B : Type u} {σ τ : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [SetLike σ A]
  [AddSubgroupClass σ A] [SetLike τ B] [AddSubgroupClass τ B] {𝒜 : ℕ → σ} {ℬ : ℕ → τ}
  [GradedRing 𝒜] [GradedRing ℬ]

private theorem exists_pow_mul_eq_zero {φ : 𝒜 →+*ᵍ ℬ} {g : A}
    (hφ : Stacks.GradedLocalization.IsAwayDegreewise φ g) {z : A} (hz : φ z = 0) :
    ∃ K : ℕ, g ^ K * z = 0 := by
  classical
  have hc : ∀ i, ∃ K : ℕ, g ^ K * (decompose 𝒜 z i : A) = 0 := fun i =>
    hφ.torsion i _ (decompose 𝒜 z i).2 (by simp [GradedRingHom.map_directSumDecompose, hz])
  choose K hK using hc
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ : ∃ N, N = ∑ i ∈ (decompose 𝒜 z).support, K i := ⟨_, rfl⟩
  refine ⟨N, ?_⟩
  have hz' := DirectSum.sum_support_decompose 𝒜 z
  calc g ^ N * z = g ^ N * ∑ i ∈ (decompose 𝒜 z).support, (decompose 𝒜 z i : A) := by
        rw [hz']
    _ = 0 := by
      rw [Finset.mul_sum]
      refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun i hi => ?_
      have hle : K i ≤ N := hN ▸ Finset.single_le_sum (fun _ _ => Nat.zero_le _) hi
      rw [← Nat.sub_add_cancel hle, pow_add, mul_assoc, hK i, mul_zero]

end GradedHom

section SectionRing

variable (s : Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.{u})

private theorem baseMap_mem (U : s.base.Opens) (r : Γ(s.base, U)) :
    s.sectionRingBaseMap U r ∈ s.sectionRingGrading U 0 :=
  ⟨_, (Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.sectionRingBaseMap_eq_of_smul_one s U r).symm⟩

/-- The `Γ(Y, U)`-algebra structure on the sections `R(U)` given by the structure map. -/
@[instance_reducible]
private noncomputable def baseAlgebra (U : s.base.Opens) :
    Algebra Γ(s.base, U) (s.sectionRing U) :=
  (show Γ(s.base, U) →+* s.sectionRing U from s.sectionRingBaseMap U).toAlgebra

attribute [local instance] baseAlgebra

/-- The degree-`n` summand of `R(U)` as a `Γ(Y, U)`-submodule. -/
private noncomputable def grading (U : s.base.Opens) (n : ℕ) :
    Submodule Γ(s.base, U) (s.sectionRing U) where
  toAddSubmonoid := (s.sectionRingGrading U n).toAddSubmonoid
  smul_mem' r x hx := by
    change s.sectionRingBaseMap U r * x ∈ s.sectionRingGrading U n
    simpa only [zero_add] using SetLike.GradedMul.mul_mem (baseMap_mem s U r) hx

/-- The grading of `R(U)` by its homogeneous summands is a graded `Γ(Y, U)`-algebra. -/
@[instance_reducible]
private noncomputable def gradingGradedAlgebra (U : s.base.Opens) :
    GradedAlgebra (grading s U) where
  one_mem := SetLike.GradedOne.one_mem (A := s.sectionRingGrading U)
  mul_mem _ _ _ _ ha hb := SetLike.GradedMul.mul_mem (A := s.sectionRingGrading U) ha hb
  decompose' := DirectSum.decompose (s.sectionRingGrading U)
  left_inv := DirectSum.Decomposition.left_inv (ℳ := s.sectionRingGrading U)
  right_inv := DirectSum.Decomposition.right_inv (ℳ := s.sectionRingGrading U)

attribute [local instance] gradingGradedAlgebra

private theorem coe_veronese (U : s.base.Opens) (d : ℕ) :
    {x : s.sectionRing U | ∀ n, ¬ d ∣ n →
      (DirectSum.decompose (s.sectionRingGrading U) x n : s.sectionRing U) = 0} =
      (MMP.Fourfold.veroneseSubalgebra (grading s U) d : Set (s.sectionRing U)) :=
  rfl

private theorem subsingleton_of_not_nonempty (U : s.base.Opens) (h : ¬ (U : Set s.base).Nonempty) :
    Subsingleton (s.sectionRing U) := by
  obtain rfl : U = ⊥ := SetLike.coe_injective (Set.not_nonempty_iff_eq_empty.mp h)
  let f : Γ(s.base, ⊥) →+* s.sectionRing ⊥ := s.sectionRingBaseMap ⊥
  refine subsingleton_of_zero_eq_one ?_
  rw [← map_zero f, ← map_one f]
  exact congrArg f (Subsingleton.elim _ _)

/-- On an affine open `U`, the section ring `R(U)` is of finite type over `Γ(Y, U)` iff its
`d`-th Veronese subring is a finitely generated `Γ(Y, U)`-subalgebra. -/
private theorem finiteType_iff_veronese_fg [IsNoetherian s.base] (U : s.base.Opens)
    (hdom : (U : Set s.base).Nonempty → IsDomain (s.sectionRing U)) (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d) :
    Algebra.FiniteType Γ(s.base, U) (s.sectionRing U) ↔
      (MMP.Fourfold.veroneseSubalgebra (grading s U) d).FG := by
  by_cases hne : (U : Set s.base).Nonempty
  · haveI := hdom hne
    haveI : IsNoetherianRing Γ(s.base, U) :=
      @IsLocallyNoetherian.component_noetherian _ IsNoetherian.toIsLocallyNoetherian ⟨U, hU⟩
    exact MMP.Fourfold.finiteType_iff_veroneseSubalgebra_fg (grading s U) hd
  · haveI := subsingleton_of_not_nonempty s U hne
    have hfg (S : Subalgebra Γ(s.base, U) (s.sectionRing U)) : S.FG :=
      Subsingleton.elim S ⊥ ▸ Subalgebra.fg_bot
    exact ⟨fun _ => hfg _, fun _ => ⟨hfg ⊤⟩⟩

/-- The subring of `R(U)` generated by `R_0(U) ∪ R_d(U)`. -/
private noncomputable def degOneSubring (d : ℕ) (U : s.base.Opens) : Subring (s.sectionRing U) :=
  Subring.closure ((s.sectionRingGrading U 0 : Set (s.sectionRing U)) ∪ s.sectionRingGrading U d)

private theorem baseMap_mem_degOneSubring (d : ℕ) (U : s.base.Opens) (r : Γ(s.base, U)) :
    s.sectionRingBaseMap U r ∈ degOneSubring s d U :=
  Subring.subset_closure (Or.inl (baseMap_mem s U r))

private theorem map_mem_degOneSubring (d : ℕ) {U V : s.base.Opens} (h : U ≤ V)
    {x : s.sectionRing V} (hx : x ∈ degOneSubring s d V) :
    s.gradedSectionRestriction U V h x ∈ degOneSubring s d U := by
  have : degOneSubring s d V ≤
      (degOneSubring s d U).comap (s.gradedSectionRestriction U V h).toRingHom :=
    Subring.closure_le.mpr fun y hy => by
      rcases hy with hy | hy
      · exact Subring.subset_closure (Or.inl ((s.gradedSectionRestriction U V h).map_mem hy))
      · exact Subring.subset_closure (Or.inr ((s.gradedSectionRestriction U V h).map_mem hy))
  exact this hx

private theorem mem_degOneSubring_of_mem_adjoin (d : ℕ) (U : s.base.Opens) {x : s.sectionRing U}
    (hx : x ∈ Algebra.adjoin Γ(s.base, U)
      ((grading s U 0 : Set (s.sectionRing U)) ∪ grading s U d)) :
    x ∈ degOneSubring s d U := by
  have hx' : x ∈ (Algebra.adjoin Γ(s.base, U)
      ((grading s U 0 : Set (s.sectionRing U)) ∪ grading s U d)).toSubring := hx
  rw [Algebra.adjoin_eq_ring_closure] at hx'
  refine (Subring.closure_le.mpr ?_) hx'
  rintro y (⟨r, rfl⟩ | hy)
  · exact baseMap_mem_degOneSubring s d U r
  · exact Subring.subset_closure hy

/-- Passing from an affine open to a basic open of it. -/
private theorem mem_degOneSubring_basicOpen (d n : ℕ) {V W : s.base.Opens} (hV : IsAffineOpen V)
    (g : Γ(s.base, V)) (hW : W = s.base.basicOpen g) (hle : W ≤ V)
    (hV' : ∀ x ∈ s.sectionRingGrading V n, x ∈ degOneSubring s d V) :
    ∀ y ∈ s.sectionRingGrading W n, y ∈ degOneSubring s d W := by
  intro y hy
  have hφ := s.isAwayDegreewise_of_eq_basicOpen hV g hW hle
  obtain ⟨j, x, hx, hxy⟩ := hφ.surj n y hy
  have hres : IsUnit (s.base.ringCatSheaf.obj.map (homOfLE hle).op g) := by
    subst hW; exact s.base.toRingedSpace.isUnit_res_basicOpen g
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := hres
  have hφg : s.gradedSectionRestriction W V hle (s.sectionRingBaseMap V g) =
      s.sectionRingBaseMap W u := by
    rw [hu]; exact s.gradedSectionRestriction_baseMap W V hle g
  have hy' : y = s.sectionRingBaseMap W (↑u⁻¹ ^ j) * s.gradedSectionRestriction W V hle x := by
    rw [hxy, hφg, ← mul_assoc, ← map_pow, ← map_mul, ← mul_pow, Units.inv_mul, one_pow, map_one,
      one_mul]
  rw [hy']
  exact (degOneSubring s d W).mul_mem (baseMap_mem_degOneSubring s d W _)
    (map_mem_degOneSubring s d hle (hV' x hx))

/-- Passing from a basic open of an affine open to the affine open, up to a power of the
function. -/
private theorem exists_pow_mul_mem_degOneSubring (d n : ℕ) {U : s.base.Opens}
    (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (f : Γ(s.base, U)) {x : s.sectionRing U}
    (hx : x ∈ s.sectionRingGrading U n)
    (hW : ∀ y ∈ s.sectionRingGrading (s.base.basicOpen f) n,
      y ∈ degOneSubring s d (s.base.basicOpen f)) :
    ∃ N : ℕ, s.sectionRingBaseMap U (f ^ (N + 1)) * x ∈ degOneSubring s d U := by
  have hφ := s.isAwayDegreewise_basicOpen f hU
  set φ := s.gradedSectionRestriction (s.base.basicOpen f) U (s.base.basicOpen_le f)
  set b := s.sectionRingBaseMap U f
  have hb : b ∈ degOneSubring s d U := baseMap_mem_degOneSubring s d U f
  let Q : Subring (s.sectionRing (s.base.basicOpen f)) :=
    { carrier := {y | ∃ J : ℕ, ∃ m ∈ degOneSubring s d U, φ b ^ J * y = φ m}
      mul_mem' := by
        rintro y₁ y₂ ⟨J₁, m₁, hm₁, h₁⟩ ⟨J₂, m₂, hm₂, h₂⟩
        exact ⟨J₁ + J₂, m₁ * m₂, mul_mem hm₁ hm₂, by rw [map_mul, ← h₁, ← h₂, pow_add]; ring⟩
      one_mem' := ⟨0, 1, one_mem _, by simp⟩
      add_mem' := by
        rintro y₁ y₂ ⟨J₁, m₁, hm₁, h₁⟩ ⟨J₂, m₂, hm₂, h₂⟩
        refine ⟨J₁ + J₂, b ^ J₂ * m₁ + b ^ J₁ * m₂,
          add_mem (mul_mem (pow_mem hb _) hm₁) (mul_mem (pow_mem hb _) hm₂), ?_⟩
        rw [map_add, map_mul, map_mul, map_pow, map_pow, ← h₁, ← h₂, pow_add]; ring
      zero_mem' := ⟨0, 0, zero_mem _, by simp⟩
      neg_mem' := by
        rintro y ⟨J, m, hm, h⟩
        exact ⟨J, -m, neg_mem hm, by rw [map_neg, ← h]; ring⟩ }
  have hQ : degOneSubring s d (s.base.basicOpen f) ≤ Q := Subring.closure_le.mpr fun y hy => by
    have key : ∀ k, y ∈ s.sectionRingGrading _ k → (k = 0 ∨ k = d) → y ∈ Q := by
      intro k hyk hk
      obtain ⟨J, m, hm, h⟩ := hφ.surj k y hyk
      refine ⟨J, m, Subring.subset_closure ?_, h.symm⟩
      rcases hk with rfl | rfl
      exacts [Or.inl hm, Or.inr hm]
    rcases hy with hy | hy
    exacts [key 0 hy (Or.inl rfl), key d hy (Or.inr rfl)]
  obtain ⟨J, m, hm, h⟩ := hQ (hW _ (φ.map_mem hx))
  obtain ⟨K, hK⟩ := exists_pow_mul_eq_zero hφ (z := b ^ J * x - m)
    (by rw [map_sub, map_mul, map_pow]; exact sub_eq_zero.mpr h)
  refine ⟨K + J, ?_⟩
  have h1 : b ^ (K + J) * x = b ^ K * m := by
    rw [pow_add, mul_assoc, ← sub_eq_zero, ← mul_sub, hK]
  have h2 : s.sectionRingBaseMap U (f ^ (K + J + 1)) * x = b * (b ^ K * m) := by
    have e : s.sectionRingBaseMap U (f ^ (K + J + 1)) = b ^ (K + J + 1) := map_pow _ _ _
    rw [e, pow_succ', mul_assoc, h1]
  rw [h2]
  exact mul_mem hb (mul_mem (pow_mem hb K) hm)

/-- Local-to-global: if every degree-`n` section over each chart of a finite affine cover lies in
the subring generated by degrees `0` and `d`, then so does every degree-`n` section over an
arbitrary affine open `U`. The functions `a` with `a ⋅ x` in that subring form an ideal containing
a power of every `f` with `D(f) ⊆ U` contained in a chart, hence the unit ideal. -/
private theorem mem_degOneSubring_of_affineCover (d n : ℕ) {t : Finset s.base.affineOpens}
    (ht : (Set.univ : Set s.base) ⊆ ⋃ V ∈ t, ((V : s.base.Opens) : Set s.base))
    (hV : ∀ V ∈ t, ∀ x ∈ s.sectionRingGrading V n, x ∈ degOneSubring s d V)
    {U : s.base.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {x : s.sectionRing U}
    (hx : x ∈ s.sectionRingGrading U n) : x ∈ degOneSubring s d U := by
  let I : Ideal Γ(s.base, U) :=
    { carrier := {a | s.sectionRingBaseMap U a * x ∈ degOneSubring s d U}
      add_mem' := fun {a b} ha hb => by
        have e : s.sectionRingBaseMap U (a + b) =
          s.sectionRingBaseMap U a + s.sectionRingBaseMap U b := map_add _ _ _
        show s.sectionRingBaseMap U (a + b) * x ∈ degOneSubring s d U
        rw [e, add_mul]; exact add_mem ha hb
      zero_mem' := by
        have e : s.sectionRingBaseMap U 0 = 0 := map_zero _
        show s.sectionRingBaseMap U 0 * x ∈ degOneSubring s d U
        rw [e, zero_mul]; exact zero_mem _
      smul_mem' := fun c a ha => by
        have e : s.sectionRingBaseMap U (c * a) =
          s.sectionRingBaseMap U c * s.sectionRingBaseMap U a := map_mul _ _ _
        show s.sectionRingBaseMap U (c * a) * x ∈ degOneSubring s d U
        rw [e, mul_assoc]
        exact mul_mem (baseMap_mem_degOneSubring s d U c) ha }
  have hI : Ideal.span (I : Set Γ(s.base, U)) = ⊤ := by
    rw [← hU.iSup_basicOpen_eq_self_iff]
    refine le_antisymm (iSup_le fun f => Scheme.basicOpen_le s.base (U := U) f.1) fun y hy => ?_
    obtain ⟨V, hVt, hyV⟩ : ∃ V ∈ t, y ∈ (V : s.base.Opens) := by
      simpa using ht (Set.mem_univ y)
    obtain ⟨f, g, hfg, hyf⟩ := exists_basicOpen_le_affine_inter hU V.2 y ⟨hy, hyV⟩
    have hle : s.base.basicOpen f ≤ V := hfg ▸ s.base.basicOpen_le g
    obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := exists_pow_mul_mem_degOneSubring s d n hU f hx
      (mem_degOneSubring_basicOpen s d n V.2 g hfg hle (hV V hVt))
    refine TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨⟨f ^ (N + 1), hN⟩, ?_⟩
    rwa [Scheme.basicOpen_pow _ _ (Nat.succ_pos N)]
  have h1 : (1 : Γ(s.base, U)) ∈ I := by
    rw [Ideal.span_eq] at hI; rw [hI]; trivial
  have e : s.sectionRingBaseMap U 1 = 1 := map_one _
  have h1' : s.sectionRingBaseMap U 1 * x ∈ degOneSubring s d U := h1
  rwa [e, one_mul] at h1'

/-- **The degree bound.** If `R` is of finite type over a quasi-compact `Y`, there is `d > 0` such
that over every affine open `U`, every section of `R_{dk}(U)` lies in the subring generated by
`R_0(U) ∪ R_d(U)`: one bound `m` on the degrees of generators serves a finite affine cover, and
`d = m * m!` works on each chart (`le_veronese`), hence on every affine open
(`mem_degOneSubring_of_affineCover`). -/
private theorem exists_forall_mem_degOneSubring [CompactSpace s.base]
    (hfin : s.IsFiniteTypeOverBase) :
    ∃ d : ℕ, 0 < d ∧ ∀ U : s.base.Opens, IsAffineOpen U → ∀ k, ∀ x ∈ s.sectionRingGrading U (d * k),
      x ∈ degOneSubring s d U := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := isCompact_univ.elim_finite_subcover
    (fun V : s.base.affineOpens => ((V : s.base.Opens) : Set s.base)) (fun V => V.1.isOpen)
    (fun y _ => by
      obtain ⟨V, hV, hyV, -⟩ := exists_isAffineOpen_mem_and_subset (x := y)
        (U := (⊤ : s.base.Opens)) trivial
      exact Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨⟨V, hV⟩, hyV⟩)
  have hm : ∀ V : s.base.affineOpens, ∃ m, 1 ≤ m ∧
      Algebra.adjoin Γ(s.base, V) (lowDeg (grading s V) m) = ⊤ := by
    intro V
    haveI : Algebra.FiniteType Γ(s.base, V) (s.sectionRing V) := hfin V V.2
    exact exists_adjoin_lowDeg_eq_top (grading s V)
  choose mV hmV1 hmV using hm
  set m := max 1 (t.sup mV)
  have hm1 : 1 ≤ m := le_max_left _ _
  refine ⟨m * m.factorial, Nat.mul_pos hm1 (Nat.factorial_pos m), ?_⟩
  set d := m * m.factorial
  have hchart : ∀ V ∈ t, ∀ k, ∀ x ∈ s.sectionRingGrading V (d * k),
      x ∈ degOneSubring s d V := by
    intro V hV k x hx
    have hgen : Algebra.adjoin Γ(s.base, V) (lowDeg (grading s V) m) = ⊤ :=
      eq_top_iff.mpr ((hmV V).symm.le.trans (Algebra.adjoin_mono
        (lowDeg_mono _ (le_max_of_le_right (Finset.le_sup hV)))))
    exact mem_degOneSubring_of_mem_adjoin s d V (le_veronese (grading s V) hm1 hgen k hx)
  exact fun U hU k x hx =>
    mem_degOneSubring_of_affineCover s d (d * k) ht (fun V hV => hchart V hV k) hU hx

end SectionRing

/-- For a Noetherian scheme `Y` and a commutative nonnegatively graded quasi-coherent
`𝒪_Y`-algebra `R` with coherent homogeneous pieces whose sections over nonempty affine opens are
integral domains, and any `d > 0`: `R` is of finite type over `𝒪_Y` if and only if, over every
affine open `U`, the Veronese ring `R^(d)(U) = ⨁_m R_{md}(U)` is a finitely generated
`Γ(Y, U)`-subalgebra of `R(U)`. -/
@[mmp "lem_mmp_foundation_km_sheaf_veronese_finite_generation"]
public theorem isFiniteTypeOverBase_iff_veronese_fg (s : Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.{u})
    [IsNoetherian s.base] (hcoh : ∀ m : ℕ, (s.algebra.piece (m : ℤ)).IsCoherent)
    (hdom : ∀ U : s.base.Opens, IsAffineOpen U → (U : Set s.base).Nonempty →
      IsDomain (s.sectionRing U))
    {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d) :
    s.IsFiniteTypeOverBase ↔
      ∀ U : s.base.Opens, IsAffineOpen U →
        letI : Algebra Γ(s.base, U) (s.sectionRing U) :=
          (show Γ(s.base, U) →+* s.sectionRing U from s.sectionRingBaseMap U).toAlgebra
        (Algebra.adjoin Γ(s.base, U)
          {x : s.sectionRing U | ∀ n, ¬ d ∣ n →
            (DirectSum.decompose (s.sectionRingGrading U) x n : s.sectionRing U) = 0}).FG := by
  refine forall₂_congr fun U hU => ?_
  letI := baseAlgebra s U
  rw [coe_veronese, Algebra.adjoin_eq]
  exact finiteType_iff_veronese_fg s U (hdom U hU) hU hd

/-- For a quasi-compact Noetherian scheme `Y` and a commutative nonnegatively graded quasi-coherent
`𝒪_Y`-algebra `R` of finite type, with coherent homogeneous pieces whose sections over nonempty
affine opens are integral domains, there is `d > 0` such that over every affine open `U` the
Veronese ring `R^(d)(U) = ⨁_m R_{md}(U)` is the `Γ(Y, U)`-subalgebra of `R(U)` generated by
`R_0(U)` and `R_d(U)`. -/
@[mmp "lem_mmp_foundation_km_sheaf_veronese_degree_one"]
public theorem exists_veronese_eq_adjoin_degree (s : Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.{u})
    [IsNoetherian s.base] [CompactSpace s.base]
    (hcoh : ∀ m : ℕ, (s.algebra.piece (m : ℤ)).IsCoherent)
    (hdom : ∀ U : s.base.Opens, IsAffineOpen U → (U : Set s.base).Nonempty →
      IsDomain (s.sectionRing U))
    (hfin : s.IsFiniteTypeOverBase) :
    ∃ d : ℕ, 0 < d ∧
      ∀ U : s.base.Opens, IsAffineOpen U →
        letI : Algebra Γ(s.base, U) (s.sectionRing U) :=
          (show Γ(s.base, U) →+* s.sectionRing U from s.sectionRingBaseMap U).toAlgebra
        Algebra.adjoin Γ(s.base, U)
            ((s.sectionRingGrading U 0 : Set (s.sectionRing U)) ∪
              (s.sectionRingGrading U d : Set (s.sectionRing U))) =
          Algebra.adjoin Γ(s.base, U)
            {x : s.sectionRing U | ∀ n, ¬ d ∣ n →
              (DirectSum.decompose (s.sectionRingGrading U) x n : s.sectionRing U) = 0} := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨d, hd, hmem⟩ := exists_forall_mem_degOneSubring s hfin
  refine ⟨d, hd, fun U hU => ?_⟩
  letI := baseAlgebra s U
  refine le_antisymm (Algebra.adjoin_le ?_) (Algebra.adjoin_le ?_)
  · rintro x (hx | hx) <;> refine Algebra.subset_adjoin fun n hn => ?_
    · exact DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_ne _ hx fun h => hn (h ▸ dvd_zero d)
    · exact DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_ne _ hx fun h => hn (h ▸ dvd_refl d)
  · intro x hx
    rw [← DirectSum.sum_support_decompose (s.sectionRingGrading U) x]
    refine Subalgebra.sum_mem _ fun n _ => ?_
    by_cases hn : d ∣ n
    · obtain ⟨k, rfl⟩ := hn
      exact (Subring.closure_le.mpr Algebra.subset_adjoin :
        degOneSubring s d U ≤ (Algebra.adjoin Γ(s.base, U) _).toSubring)
        (hmem U hU k _ (decompose _ x (d * k)).2)
    · rw [hx n hn]; exact zero_mem _

end MMP.Fourfold

namespace MMP.Mori.Divisor

open MMP.Fourfold

/-- If every point of coheight at most one maps into the biregular locus of `g`, then the
exceptional set of `g` has codimension at least two. -/
private theorem two_le_closedsCodimension_exceptionalSet_of_coheight_le_one {X Y : Scheme.{u}}
    (g : X ⟶ Y) (h : ∀ x : X, Order.coheight x ≤ 1 → g x ∈ biregularLocus g) :
    2 ≤ closedsCodimension (exceptionalSet g) :=
  MMP.Flips.le_closedsCodimension_iff_le_coheight.mpr fun x hx =>
    not_lt.mp fun hlt => hx (h x (Order.le_of_lt_succ hlt))

/-- For the relative `Proj` of a divisorial algebra `⨁_{m ≥ 0} 𝒪_Y(m e B)` generated in degree one,
`g⁻¹_*(e B)` is Cartier: on each chart `D₊(a)` the pull-back of `a⁻¹` is a local equation
(`MMP.Fourfold.DivisorialSectionAlgebra.isCartier_inverseTransformDivisor`). -/
private theorem isCartier_inverseTransformDivisor_of_divisorialSectionAlgebra
    {k : Type u} [Field k]
    {Y : Scheme.{u}} {sY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k)} [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [IsNormal Y] [CompactSpace Y]
    (hY : IsNormalVariety k sY) (B : Divisor Y) (e : ℕ)
    (hgen : ∀ V : Y.Opens, IsAffineOpen V → ∀ n : ℕ,
      ((n : ℤ) • (e • B)).divisorialSubmodule V ≤ (((1 : ℤ) • (e • B)).divisorialSubmodule V) ^ n)
    [IsLocallyNoetherian (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProj]
    [IsNormal (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProj]
    (hZ : IsNormalVariety k ((divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProjToBase ≫ sY))
    (hbir : IsBirationalMorphism (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProjToBase) :
    Divisor.IsCartier (X := (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProj)
      (inverseTransformDivisor (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProjToBase
        (e • B)) := by
  have : IsIntegral Y := hY.1.toIsIntegral
  have : IsIntegral (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).model := hZ.1.toIsIntegral
  have : IsDominant (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).toBase := hbir.isDominant
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).model :=
    ‹IsLocallyNoetherian (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProj›
  have : IsNormal (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).model :=
    ‹IsNormal (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProj›
  exact MMP.Fourfold.DivisorialSectionAlgebra.isCartier_inverseTransformDivisor
    (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)) (isLocallyDegreeOneGenerated_divisorialSectionAlgebra
      (e • B) hgen)

/-- For the relative `Proj` of a divisorial algebra `⨁_{m ≥ 0} 𝒪_Y(m e B)` generated in degree one,
the restriction of `𝒪_Z(g⁻¹_*(e B))` to the chart over an affine open `W` is the twisting sheaf
`𝒪(1)` of the chart. -/
private theorem nonempty_restrict_iso_twistingSheaf_of_divisorialSectionAlgebra
    {k : Type u} [Field k]
    {Y : Scheme.{u}} {sY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k)} [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [IsNormal Y] [CompactSpace Y]
    (hY : IsNormalVariety k sY) (B : Divisor Y) (e : ℕ)
    (hgen : ∀ V : Y.Opens, IsAffineOpen V → ∀ n : ℕ,
      ((n : ℤ) • (e • B)).divisorialSubmodule V ≤ (((1 : ℤ) • (e • B)).divisorialSubmodule V) ^ n)
    [CompactSpace (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProj]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProj]
    [IsNormal (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProj]
    (hZ : IsNormalVariety k ((divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProjToBase ≫ sY))
    (hbir : IsBirationalMorphism (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProjToBase)
    (W : (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.base.affineOpens) :
    Nonempty (Scheme.Modules.restrict (Divisor.divisorialSheaf
        (X := (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProj)
        (inverseTransformDivisor (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProjToBase
          (e • B))) ((divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProjChart W) ≅
      ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.twistingSheaf
        ((divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.sectionRingGrading W.1) 1) := by
  have : IsIntegral Y := hY.1.toIsIntegral
  have : IsIntegral (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).model := hZ.1.toIsIntegral
  have : IsDominant (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).toBase := hbir.isDominant
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).model :=
    ‹IsLocallyNoetherian (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProj›
  have : IsNormal (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).model :=
    ‹IsNormal (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProj›
  have : CompactSpace (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).model :=
    ‹CompactSpace (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProj›
  let j : AlgebraicGeometry.Proj ((divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.sectionRingGrading
      W.1) ⟶ (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).model :=
    (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProjChart W
  have hj : IsOpenImmersion j :=
    Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.isOpenImmersion_relativeProjChart _ W
  exact DivisorialSectionAlgebra.nonempty_restrict_divisorialSheaf_iso_twistingSheaf_of_transition
    (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)) W.2
    (isLocallyDegreeOneGenerated_divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B) hgen W.1) j rfl
    (fun a b φ ψ _ hb hφ hψ =>
      MMP.Fourfold.DivisorialSectionAlgebra.algebraMap_fracSection_mul_pullbackRationalFunction_eq
        (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)) W.2 j hj rfl a b hb φ ψ hφ hψ)

/-- **The relative `Proj` of a divisorial algebra generated in degree one is a small ample
model.** Let `g : Z = Proj_Y ⨁_{m ≥ 0} 𝒪_Y(m e B) ⟶ Y` with the algebra generated in degree one
and `𝒪(1)` relatively ample. Then the exceptional set of `g` has codimension at least two (`g`
is an isomorphism over the points of codimension at most one), and `g⁻¹_* B` is `ℚ`-Cartier and
`g`-ample: `e g⁻¹_* B = g⁻¹_*(e B)` is Cartier, with `𝒪_Z(g⁻¹_*(e B))` equal to `𝒪(1)` on every
chart. -/
private theorem small_of_divisorialSectionAlgebra {k : Type u} [Field k]
    {Y : Scheme.{u}} {sY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k)} [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [IsNormal Y] [CompactSpace Y]
    (hY : IsNormalVariety k sY) (B : Divisor Y) (e : ℕ) (he : 0 < e)
    (hgen : ∀ V : Y.Opens, IsAffineOpen V → ∀ n : ℕ,
      ((n : ℤ) • (e • B)).divisorialSubmodule V ≤ (((1 : ℤ) • (e • B)).divisorialSubmodule V) ^ n)
    [CompactSpace (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProj]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProj]
    [IsNormal (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProj]
    (hZ : IsNormalVariety k ((divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProjToBase ≫ sY))
    (hbir : IsBirationalMorphism (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProjToBase)
    [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProj
      ((divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.twistSheaf 1)]
    (hamp : Stacks.RelativeAmple.IsRelativelyAmple
      (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProjToBase
      ((divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.twistSheaf 1)) :
    2 ≤ closedsCodimension (exceptionalSet
        (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProjToBase) ∧
      (Divisor.toQDivisor (inverseTransformDivisor
        (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProjToBase B)).IsQCartier ∧
      (Divisor.toQDivisor (inverseTransformDivisor
        (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProjToBase B)).HasRelativelyAmpleMultiple
        (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProjToBase := by
  have : IsIntegral Y := hY.1.toIsIntegral
  have hL := isCartier_inverseTransformDivisor_of_divisorialSectionAlgebra hY B e hgen hZ hbir
  have heq : Divisor.toQDivisor (inverseTransformDivisor
      (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProjToBase (e • B)) =
      ((e : ℕ) : ℤ) • Divisor.toQDivisor (inverseTransformDivisor
        (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.relativeProjToBase B) := by
    rw [map_nsmul, map_nsmul, natCast_zsmul]
  haveI := hL.isInvertibleModule_divisorialSheaf
  exact ⟨two_le_closedsCodimension_exceptionalSet_of_coheight_le_one _ fun z hz =>
      MMP.Fourfold.DivisorialSectionAlgebra.toBase_mem_biregularLocus_of_coheight_le_one
        (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B))
        (isLocallyDegreeOneGenerated_divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B) hgen) z hz,
    ⟨e, by exact_mod_cast he.ne', _, heq, hL⟩, e, he, _, hL, heq,
    MMP.Mori.isRelativelyAmple_of_restrict_projectiveConeChart_iso _ _ hamp fun W =>
      nonempty_restrict_iso_twistingSheaf_of_divisorialSectionAlgebra hY B e hgen hZ hbir W⟩

variable {k : Type u} [Field k] {Y : Scheme.{u}} {sY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k)}
  [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [IsNormal Y]

/-- **KM Lemma 6.2, (1) ⇒ (2).** Let `Y` be a normal variety over `k` and `B` a Weil divisor on
`Y` such that the divisorial algebra `R(Y, B) = ⊕_{m ≥ 0} 𝒪_Y(mB)` is a sheaf of finitely
generated `𝒪_Y`-algebras. Then there is a projective birational morphism `g : Z ⟶ Y` over `k`
from a normal variety `Z`, with exceptional set of codimension at least two in `Z`, such that
the birational transform `g⁻¹_* B` is `ℚ`-Cartier and `g`-ample. -/
@[mmp "lem_km3c_reflexive_algebra_fg_implies_small_model"]
public theorem exists_isSmallAmpleModel_of_finiteType_divisorialAlgebra
    (hY : IsNormalVariety k sY) (B : Divisor Y)
    (hR : ∀ y : Y, ∃ U : Y.Opens, IsAffineOpen U ∧ y ∈ U ∧
      Algebra.FiniteType Γ(Y, U) (B.divisorialAlgebraSections U)) :
    ∃ (Z : Scheme.{u}) (_ : CompactSpace Z) (_ : IsLocallyNoetherian Z) (_ : IsNormal Z)
      (sZ : Z ⟶ Spec (.of k)) (g : Z ⟶ Y),
      IsNormalVariety k sZ ∧ g ≫ sY = sZ ∧ AlgebraicGeometry.IsProjective g ∧
        IsBirationalMorphism g ∧ 2 ≤ closedsCodimension (exceptionalSet g) ∧
        (Divisor.toQDivisor (inverseTransformDivisor g B)).IsQCartier ∧
        (Divisor.toQDivisor (inverseTransformDivisor g B)).HasRelativelyAmpleMultiple g := by
  have : AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety k sY := hY.1
  have : IsIntegral Y := hY.1.toIsIntegral
  have : QuasiCompact sY := hY.1.toQuasiCompact
  have : CompactSpace Y := (quasiCompact_iff_compactSpace sY).mp inferInstance
  have : IsNoetherian Y := { }
  have hcohD (D : Divisor Y) : SheafOfModules.IsCoherent D.divisorialSheaf :=
    (MMP.Threefold.isCoherent_divisorialSheaf_and_isIso_divisorialSheafTensorMul sY hY.1 D 0).1
  -- the Veronese degree `e` in which `R(Y, B)` is generated
  obtain ⟨e, he, hve⟩ := MMP.Fourfold.exists_veronese_eq_adjoin_degree
    (divisorialSectionAlgebra B).situation (fun m => hcohD _)
    (fun U _ hU => (divisorialSectionAlgebra B).isDomain_sectionRing U hU)
    (fun U hU => (divisorialSectionAlgebra B).finiteType_sectionRingBaseMap U
      (B.finiteType_divisorialAlgebraSections_of_forall_exists hR hU))
  have hgen : ∀ V : Y.Opens, IsAffineOpen V → ∀ n : ℕ,
      ((n : ℤ) • (e • B)).divisorialSubmodule V ≤
        (((1 : ℤ) • (e • B)).divisorialSubmodule V) ^ n := fun V hV n => by
    letI : Algebra Γ(Y, V) ((divisorialSectionAlgebra B).situation.sectionRing V) :=
      (show Γ(Y, V) →+* (divisorialSectionAlgebra B).situation.sectionRing V from
        (divisorialSectionAlgebra B).situation.sectionRingBaseMap V).toAlgebra
    exact divisorialSubmodule_le_pow_of_adjoin_eq B he (fun _ => rfl) (hve V hV) n
  have hcoh1 : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsCoherent ((sectionGradedAlgebra (e • B)).piece 1) :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentAbelian.stacksIsCoherent_of_isCoherent (hcohD _)
  set R := (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation
  have hRc : MMP.Intersection.Scheme.IsConeAlgebra R :=
    isConeAlgebra_divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B) hcoh1 hgen
  -- `R(Y, e B)` is of finite type on every affine open
  have hA : ∀ U : Y.Opens, IsAffineOpen U →
      ((divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).situation.sectionRingBaseMap U).FiniteType := by
    intro U hU
    haveI : (((1 : ℤ) • (e • B)).divisorialSheaf).IsFiniteType := (hcohD _).isFiniteType
    haveI : (((1 : ℤ) • (e • B)).divisorialSheaf).IsQuasicoherent :=
      isQuasicoherent_divisorialSheaf _
    have hfin : Module.Finite Γ(Y, U) (((1 : ℤ) • (e • B)).divisorialSubmodule U) :=
      AlgebraicGeometry.finite_sections_of_isAffineOpen ((1 : ℤ) • (e • B)).divisorialSheaf U hU
    exact (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).finiteType_sectionRingBaseMap U
      (finiteType_divisorialAlgebraSections_of_le_pow (e • B) hfin (hgen U hU))
  have hZ : IsNormalVariety k (R.relativeProjToBase ≫ sY) :=
    MMP.Fourfold.DivisorialSectionAlgebra.isNormalVariety_model sY hY B e he
      (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)) hA
  obtain ⟨hproj, ⟨hinv, hamp⟩, -⟩ :=
    MMP.Foundations.ConeAlgebra.isProjective_and_isIso_pieceToPushforwardTwist R hRc
      (fun n => AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentAbelian.stacksIsCoherent_of_isCoherent (hcohD _))
      (fun U hU => (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).isDomain_sectionRing U
        (Set.nonempty_coe_sort.mp hU))
  haveI := hinv
  have : AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety k (R.relativeProjToBase ≫ sY) := hZ.1
  have : IsNormal R.relativeProj := hZ.2
  have : QuasiCompact (R.relativeProjToBase ≫ sY) := hZ.1.toQuasiCompact
  have : CompactSpace R.relativeProj :=
    (quasiCompact_iff_compactSpace (R.relativeProjToBase ≫ sY)).mp inferInstance
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian R.relativeProj :=
    LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian (R.relativeProjToBase ≫ sY)
  have : IsIntegral R.relativeProj := hZ.1.toIsIntegral
  have : IrreducibleSpace (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B)).model :=
    (inferInstance : IrreducibleSpace R.relativeProj)
  have hbir : IsBirationalMorphism R.relativeProjToBase :=
    MMP.Fourfold.DivisorialSectionAlgebra.isBirationalMorphism_toBase
      (divisorialSectionAlgebra (e • B))
  exact ⟨R.relativeProj, inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance, R.relativeProjToBase ≫ sY,
    R.relativeProjToBase, hZ, rfl, hproj, hbir,
    small_of_divisorialSectionAlgebra hY B e he hgen hZ hbir hamp⟩

end MMP.Mori.Divisor

namespace MMP.Mori

open Opposite TopologicalSpace

section RationalFunctions

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X]

private theorem germ_eq_rationalFunctionsEquivFunctionField_symm (U : X.Opens) (s : Γ(X, U))
    (h : genericPoint X ∈ U) (Z : irreducibleComponents X) (hZ : componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ U) :
    (rationalFunctionsEquivFunctionField X).symm (X.presheaf.germ U (genericPoint X) h s) Z =
      X.presheaf.germ U (componentGenericPoint X Z) hZ s := by
  haveI : Finite (irreducibleComponents X) := by
    rw [irreducibleComponents_eq_singleton]
    infer_instance
  have hd : Dense (U : Set X) := U.isOpen.dense ⟨_, h⟩
  let D : Stacks.Chow.DenseOpen X := ⟨U, hd⟩
  have key : (rationalFunctionsEquivFunctionField X).symm (X.presheaf.germ U (genericPoint X) h s)
      = (Stacks.Chow.rationalFunctionsEquivStalks X).1 (Stacks.Chow.ofSection X D s) := by
    rw [RingEquiv.symm_apply_eq, ← (Stacks.Chow.rationalFunctionsEquivFunctionField X).2 D s h]
    change _ = (Stacks.Chow.rationalFunctionsEquivFunctionField X).1
      ((Stacks.Chow.rationalFunctionsEquivStalks X).1.symm _)
    rw [RingEquiv.symm_apply_apply]
  rw [key]
  exact (Stacks.Chow.rationalFunctionsEquivStalks X).2 D s Z hZ

/-- A rational function, seen as a section of `𝒦_X` over `U`. -/
private noncomputable def toSections (U : X.Opens) :
    X.functionField →+* (rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op U) :=
  ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).map (homOfLE le_top : U ⟶ ⊤).op).hom.comp
    ((rationalFunctionsPresheafTopEquiv X).symm.toRingHom.comp
      (rationalFunctionsEquivFunctionField X).symm.toRingHom)

private theorem bijective_toSections (U : X.Opens) (hU : genericPoint X ∈ U) :
    Function.Bijective (toSections U) := by
  have hmem (Z : irreducibleComponents X) : componentGenericPoint X Z ∈ U :=
    (MMP.Fourfold.componentGenericPoint_eq_genericPoint Z) ▸ hU
  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · intro φ ψ h
    apply (rationalFunctionsEquivFunctionField X).symm.injective
    apply (rationalFunctionsPresheafTopEquiv X).symm.injective
    funext Z
    exact congrFun h ⟨Z.1, hmem Z.1⟩
  · intro s
    refine ⟨(rationalFunctionsEquivFunctionField X) ((rationalFunctionsPresheafTopEquiv X)
      (fun Z => s ⟨Z.1, hmem Z.1⟩)), ?_⟩
    funext Z
    simp only [toSections, RingHom.comp_apply, RingEquiv.toRingHom_eq_coe,
      RingEquiv.coe_toRingHom, RingEquiv.symm_apply_apply]
    rfl

private noncomputable def sectionsEquiv (U : X.Opens) (hU : genericPoint X ∈ U) :
    X.functionField ≃+* (rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op U) :=
  RingEquiv.ofBijective (toSections U) (bijective_toSections U hU)

private theorem sectionsEquiv_germ (U : X.Opens) (hU : genericPoint X ∈ U) (a : Γ(X, U)) :
    sectionsEquiv U hU (X.presheaf.germ U (genericPoint X) hU a) =
      algebraMap Γ(X, U) ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf X).obj (op U)) a := by
  funext Z
  exact germ_eq_rationalFunctionsEquivFunctionField_symm U a hU Z.1 Z.2

end RationalFunctions

private theorem roundDown_smul_toQDivisor {X : Scheme.{u}} (D : Divisor X) (m : ℕ) :
    DivisorWithCoeffs.roundDown ((m : ℚ) • Divisor.toQDivisor D) = m • D := by
  ext E
  simp only [DivisorWithCoeffs.coeff_roundDown, DivisorWithCoeffs.coeff_smul]
  simp
  exact_mod_cast Int.floor_intCast ((m : ℤ) * D.coeff E)

private theorem functionFieldMap_germ {Y Z : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral Y] [IsIntegral Z] (g : Z ⟶ Y)
    [IsDominant g] (U : Y.Opens) (hY : genericPoint Y ∈ U) (hZ : genericPoint Z ∈ g ⁻¹ᵁ U)
    (a : Γ(Y, U)) :
    functionFieldMap g (Y.presheaf.germ U (genericPoint Y) hY a) =
      Z.presheaf.germ (g ⁻¹ᵁ U) (genericPoint Z) hZ (g.app U a) := by
  rw [functionFieldMap, CommRingCat.hom_comp, RingHom.comp_apply,
    ← Scheme.Hom.germ_stalkMap_apply g U _ hZ]
  congr 1
  rw [TopCat.Presheaf.stalkCongr_hom]
  exact TopCat.Presheaf.germ_stalkSpecializes_apply _ _ _ _

private theorem bijective_functionFieldMap {Y Z : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral Y] [IsIntegral Z]
    (g : Z ⟶ Y) [IsDominant g] (hEx : 2 ≤ closedsCodimension (exceptionalSet g)) :
    Function.Bijective (functionFieldMap g) := by
  have hgen : g (genericPoint Z) ∈ biregularLocus g := by
    by_contra h
    have := MMP.Positivity.two_le_coheight_of_mem_exceptionalSet hEx (mem_exceptionalSet.mpr h)
    rw [Order.coheight_eq_zero.mpr (fun z _ => genericPoint_specializes z)] at this
    exact absurd this (by decide)
  haveI := MMP.Threefold.Resolution.isIso_stalkMap_of_mem_biregularLocus g hgen
  exact ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso _

/-- Over an open `U` not containing the generic point, `𝒦_Y(U) = 0`, so the divisorial algebra
is trivially of finite type. -/
private theorem finiteType_divisorialAlgebraSections_of_genericPoint_notMem {Y : Scheme.{u}}
    [IsIntegral Y] [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [IsNormal Y] (B : Divisor Y) (U : Y.Opens)
    (hne : genericPoint Y ∉ U) :
    Algebra.FiniteType Γ(Y, U) (B.divisorialAlgebraSections U) := by
  haveI : IsEmpty {E : irreducibleComponents Y // componentGenericPoint Y E ∈ U} :=
    ⟨fun E => hne (MMP.Fourfold.componentGenericPoint_eq_genericPoint E.1 ▸ E.2)⟩
  haveI : Subsingleton ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf Y).obj (op U)) := by
    change Subsingleton (∀ E : {E : irreducibleComponents Y // componentGenericPoint Y E ∈ U}, _)
    infer_instance
  haveI : Subsingleton (B.divisorialAlgebraSections U) :=
    ⟨fun p q => Subtype.ext (Subsingleton.elim _ _)⟩
  exact ⟨⟨∅, eq_top_iff.mpr fun x _ => Subsingleton.elim x 0 ▸ Subalgebra.zero_mem _⟩⟩

/-- Finite generation transports along a ring isomorphism `Φ : 𝒦_Y(U) ≃+* S`: if `Φ` carries
each `𝒪_Y(mB)(U)` onto a set `N m`, and the constants `f a` pull back to `Γ(Y, U)`, then a finite
set `G ⊆ S[t]` with coefficients in `N` which, together with the constants `f a`, generates every
polynomial with coefficients in `N`, pulls back to generators of `R(Y, B)(U)`. -/
private theorem finiteType_divisorialAlgebraSections_of_ringEquiv {Y : Scheme.{u}}
    [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [IsNormal Y] (B : Divisor Y) (U : Y.Opens) {S : Type*} [CommRing S]
    (Φ : (rationalFunctionsPresheaf Y).obj (op U) ≃+* S) (N : ℕ → Set S) (f : Γ(Y, U) → S)
    (hΦ : ∀ (m : ℕ) x, x ∈ (m • B).divisorialSubmodule U ↔ Φ x ∈ N m)
    (hf : ∀ a, Φ.symm (f a) = algebraMap Γ(Y, U) _ a) (G : Finset (Polynomial S))
    (hG : ∀ q ∈ G, ∀ m, q.coeff m ∈ N m)
    (hgen : ∀ p : Polynomial S, (∀ m, p.coeff m ∈ N m) →
      p ∈ Subring.closure (Set.range (fun a => Polynomial.C (f a)) ∪ ↑G)) :
    Algebra.FiniteType Γ(Y, U) (B.divisorialAlgebraSections U) := by
  classical
  let P := Polynomial.mapRingHom Φ.symm.toRingHom
  have hPG : ∀ q ∈ G, P q ∈ B.divisorialAlgebraSections U := fun q hq m => by
    change (q.map Φ.symm.toRingHom).coeff m ∈ _
    rw [Polynomial.coeff_map]
    exact (hΦ m _).mpr (by simpa using hG q hq m)
  have hS : B.divisorialAlgebraSections U = Algebra.adjoin Γ(Y, U) (P '' G) := by
    refine le_antisymm (fun p hp => ?_) (Algebra.adjoin_le ?_)
    · have hp' := hgen (p.map Φ.toRingHom) fun m => by
        rw [Polynomial.coeff_map]
        exact (hΦ m _).mp (hp m)
      have hPp : P (p.map Φ.toRingHom) = p := by
        change Polynomial.map _ (Polynomial.map _ p) = p
        rw [Polynomial.map_map, RingEquiv.symm_toRingHom_comp_toRingHom, Polynomial.map_id]
      have : P (p.map Φ.toRingHom) ∈ (Subring.closure _).map P := Subring.mem_map.mpr ⟨_, hp', rfl⟩
      rw [RingHom.map_closure, hPp] at this
      refine (Subring.closure_le (t := (Algebra.adjoin Γ(Y, U) (P '' G)).toSubring)).mpr ?_ this
      rintro _ ⟨x, ⟨a, rfl⟩ | hx, rfl⟩
      · have : P (Polynomial.C (f a)) = algebraMap Γ(Y, U) _ a := by
          simp [P, hf, Polynomial.algebraMap_apply]
        rw [this]
        exact Subalgebra.algebraMap_mem _ a
      · exact Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    · rintro _ ⟨q, hq, rfl⟩
      exact hPG q hq
  exact ⟨(Subalgebra.fg_top _).mpr ⟨G.image P, by rw [Finset.coe_image, ← hS]⟩⟩

/-- **KM Lemma 6.2, (2) ⇒ (1), the transport step.** For `g : Z ⟶ Y` proper dominant with
exceptional set of codimension at least two, `𝒦_Y(U) ≅ 𝒦_Z(g⁻¹U)` carries `𝒪_Y(mB)(U)` onto
`𝒪_Z(m g⁻¹_* B)(g⁻¹U)`; so a finite set `G` generating, with the constants from `Γ(Y, U)`, the
polynomials over `𝒦_Z(g⁻¹U)` with coefficients in `𝒪_Z(m g⁻¹_* B)(g⁻¹U)` gives generators of
`R(Y, B)(U)`. -/
private theorem finiteType_divisorialAlgebraSections_of_finset_closure {Y Z : Scheme.{u}}
    [IsIntegral Y] [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [IsNormal Y] [IsIntegral Z] [IsLocallyNoetherian Z]
    [IsNormal Z] (g : Z ⟶ Y) [IsProper g] [IsDominant g]
    (hEx : 2 ≤ closedsCodimension (exceptionalSet g)) (B : Divisor Y) (U : Y.Opens)
    (G : Finset (Polynomial ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf Z).obj (op (g ⁻¹ᵁ U)))))
    (hG : ∀ p ∈ G, ∀ m : ℕ, p.coeff m ∈ (DivisorWithCoeffs.roundDown
      ((m : ℚ) • Divisor.toQDivisor (inverseTransformDivisor g B))).divisorialSubmodule (g ⁻¹ᵁ U))
    (hgen : ∀ p : Polynomial ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf Z).obj (op (g ⁻¹ᵁ U))),
      (∀ m : ℕ, p.coeff m ∈ (DivisorWithCoeffs.roundDown
        ((m : ℚ) • Divisor.toQDivisor (inverseTransformDivisor g B))).divisorialSubmodule
          (g ⁻¹ᵁ U)) →
      p ∈ Subring.closure (Set.range (fun a : Γ(Y, U) =>
        Polynomial.C (algebraMap Γ(Z, g ⁻¹ᵁ U)
          ((rationalFunctionsPresheaf Z).obj (op (g ⁻¹ᵁ U))) (g.app U a))) ∪ ↑G)) :
    Algebra.FiniteType Γ(Y, U) (B.divisorialAlgebraSections U) := by
  by_cases hne : genericPoint Y ∈ U
  swap
  · exact finiteType_divisorialAlgebraSections_of_genericPoint_notMem B U hne
  have hgZ : genericPoint Z ∈ g ⁻¹ᵁ U := by
    obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := g.denseRange.exists_mem_open U.isOpen ⟨_, hne⟩
    exact ((genericPoint_spec Z).mem_open_set_iff (g ⁻¹ᵁ U).isOpen).mpr ⟨z, trivial, hz⟩
  let eY := sectionsEquiv U hne
  let eZ := sectionsEquiv (g ⁻¹ᵁ U) hgZ
  let Φ := eY.symm.trans ((RingEquiv.ofBijective _ (bijective_functionFieldMap g hEx)).trans eZ)
  refine finiteType_divisorialAlgebraSections_of_ringEquiv B U Φ
    (fun m => (DivisorWithCoeffs.roundDown ((m : ℚ) •
      Divisor.toQDivisor (inverseTransformDivisor g B))).divisorialSubmodule (g ⁻¹ᵁ U))
    _ (fun m x => ?_) (fun a => ?_) G hG hgen
  · rw [roundDown_smul_toQDivisor, ← map_nsmul]
    conv_lhs => rw [← eY.apply_symm_apply x]
    exact Divisor.mem_divisorialSubmodule_inverseTransformDivisor_iff g hEx (m • B) U (eY.symm x)
  · rw [RingEquiv.symm_apply_eq, ← sectionsEquiv_germ U hne a, ← sectionsEquiv_germ _ hgZ]
    change _ = eZ (functionFieldMap g (eY.symm (eY _)))
    rw [RingEquiv.symm_apply_apply, functionFieldMap_germ g U hne hgZ]

/-- **KM Lemma 6.2, (2) ⇒ (1).** Let `g : Z ⟶ Y` be a proper dominant morphism of locally
Noetherian normal integral schemes whose exceptional set has codimension at least two, and `B`
a divisor on `Y` such that the birational transform `g⁻¹_* B` is `ℚ`-Cartier and `g`-ample.
Then the divisorial algebra `R(Y, B) = ⊕_{m ≥ 0} 𝒪_Y(mB)` is a sheaf of finitely generated
`𝒪_Y`-algebras: over every affine open `U ⊆ Y`, its sections `B.divisorialAlgebraSections U`
form a finitely generated `Γ(Y, U)`-algebra. -/
@[mmp "lem_km3c_small_model_implies_reflexive_algebra_fg"]
public theorem Divisor.finiteType_divisorialAlgebraSections_of_inverseTransformDivisor
    {Y Z : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral Y] [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [IsNormal Y]
    [IsIntegral Z] [IsLocallyNoetherian Z] [IsNormal Z] [CompactSpace Z] (g : Z ⟶ Y)
    [IsProper g] [IsDominant g] (hEx : 2 ≤ closedsCodimension (exceptionalSet g))
    (B : Divisor Y)
    (hB : (Divisor.toQDivisor (inverseTransformDivisor g B)).HasRelativelyAmpleMultiple g)
    (U : Y.Opens) (hU : IsAffineOpen U) :
    Algebra.FiniteType Γ(Y, U) (B.divisorialAlgebraSections U) := by
  obtain ⟨G, hG, hgen⟩ :=
    QDivisor.exists_finset_closure_roundDown_eq_of_hasRelativelyAmpleMultiple g
      (Divisor.toQDivisor (inverseTransformDivisor g B))
      (by obtain ⟨m, hm, L, hL, hLeq, -⟩ := hB; exact ⟨m, by exact_mod_cast hm.ne', L, hLeq, hL⟩)
      hB U hU
  exact finiteType_divisorialAlgebraSections_of_finset_closure g hEx B U G hG hgen

/-- **KM Lemma 6.2, (2) ⇒ (1), with a relatively free transform.** Let `g : Z ⟶ Y` be a
projective dominant morphism of locally Noetherian normal integral schemes whose exceptional set
has codimension at least two, and `B` a divisor on `Y` such that for some `d > 0` the divisor
`d g⁻¹_* B` is Cartier and `g`-free (`g^* g_* 𝒪_Z(d g⁻¹_* B) → 𝒪_Z(d g⁻¹_* B)` is surjective).
Then over every affine open `U ⊆ Y` the sections `B.divisorialAlgebraSections U` of the
divisorial algebra `R(Y, B)` form a finitely generated `Γ(Y, U)`-algebra. -/
public theorem Divisor.finiteType_divisorialAlgebraSections_of_isRelativelyFreeDivisor
    {Y Z : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral Y] [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [IsNormal Y]
    [IsIntegral Z] [IsLocallyNoetherian Z] [IsNormal Z] [CompactSpace Z] (g : Z ⟶ Y)
    (hg : AlgebraicGeometry.IsProjective g) [IsDominant g]
    (hEx : 2 ≤ closedsCodimension (exceptionalSet g)) (B : Divisor Y) {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d)
    (hL : Divisor.IsCartier (d • inverseTransformDivisor g B))
    (hfree : MMP.Fourfold.IsRelativelyFreeDivisor g (d • inverseTransformDivisor g B))
    (U : Y.Opens) (hU : IsAffineOpen U) :
    Algebra.FiniteType Γ(Y, U) (B.divisorialAlgebraSections U) := by
  haveI : IsProper g := hg.isProper
  obtain ⟨G, hG, hgen⟩ :=
    QDivisor.exists_finset_closure_roundDown_eq_of_isRelativelyFreeDivisor g hg
      (Divisor.toQDivisor (inverseTransformDivisor g B)) hd _
      (by rw [map_nsmul, natCast_zsmul]) hL hfree U hU
  exact finiteType_divisorialAlgebraSections_of_finset_closure g hEx B U G hG hgen

/-- A prime divisor with integer coefficient, regarded as a `ℚ`-divisor. -/
private theorem toQDivisor_single {X : Scheme.{u}} (E : Mori.PrimeDivisor X) (m : ℤ) :
    Divisor.toQDivisor (Finsupp.single E m) = Finsupp.single E (m : ℚ) :=
  Finsupp.mapRange_single (hf := map_zero _)

/-- Mapping prime divisors commutes with regarding a divisor as a `ℚ`-divisor. -/
private theorem mapPrimeDivisors_toQDivisor {X Y : Scheme.{u}}
    (φ : Mori.PrimeDivisor X → Option (Mori.PrimeDivisor Y)) (K : Divisor X) :
    DivisorWithCoeffs.mapPrimeDivisors φ (Divisor.toQDivisor K) =
      Divisor.toQDivisor (DivisorWithCoeffs.mapPrimeDivisors φ K) := by
  induction K using Finsupp.induction_linear with
  | zero => simp
  | add A B hA hB => simp only [map_add, hA, hB]
  | single P n =>
    rw [toQDivisor_single, DivisorWithCoeffs.mapPrimeDivisors_single,
      DivisorWithCoeffs.mapPrimeDivisors_single]
    cases φ P with
    | none => simp
    | some E => simp [toQDivisor_single]

/-- The birational transform `g⁻¹_* f_*` commutes with regarding a divisor as a `ℚ`-divisor. -/
private theorem flipTransform_toQDivisor {X Y Z : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y) (g : Z ⟶ Y)
    (K : Divisor X) :
    flipTransform f g (Divisor.toQDivisor K) = Divisor.toQDivisor (flipTransform f g K) := by
  simp only [flipTransform, AddMonoidHom.comp_apply, RationalMap.transformDivisor,
    inverseTransformDivisor, mapPrimeDivisors_toQDivisor]

/-- A `ℚ`-divisor is `ℚ`-Cartier as soon as a positive integral multiple of it is. -/
private theorem isQCartier_of_natCast_smul {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X]
    {E : QDivisor X} {r : ℕ} (hr : 0 < r) (h : ((r : ℤ) • E).IsQCartier) : E.IsQCartier := by
  obtain ⟨m, hm, h⟩ := h
  exact ⟨m * r, mul_ne_zero hm (by exact_mod_cast hr.ne'), by rwa [mul_smul]⟩

/-- A `ℚ`-divisor is `g`-ample as soon as a positive integral multiple of it is. -/
private theorem hasRelativelyAmpleMultiple_of_natCast_smul {X Y : Scheme.{u}} [CompactSpace X]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X] {E : QDivisor X} {g : X ⟶ Y} {r : ℕ} (hr : 0 < r)
    (h : ((r : ℤ) • E).HasRelativelyAmpleMultiple g) : E.HasRelativelyAmpleMultiple g := by
  obtain ⟨m, hm, L, hL, hLe, hamp⟩ := h
  refine ⟨m * r, Nat.mul_pos hm hr, L, hL, ?_, hamp⟩
  rw [hLe, ← mul_smul]; push_cast; rfl

/-- The transform `g⁻¹_* f_*(rK + Dr)` of `rK + rD` is `r(K_Z + D_Z)`. -/
private theorem toQDivisor_flipTransform_eq {X Y Z : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y) (g : Z ⟶ Y)
    (K : Divisor X) (D : QDivisor X) (r : ℕ) (Dr : Divisor X)
    (hDr : Divisor.toQDivisor Dr = (r : ℚ) • D) :
    Divisor.toQDivisor (flipTransform f g (r • K + Dr)) =
      (r : ℤ) • (Divisor.toQDivisor (flipTransform f g K) + flipTransform f g D) := by
  rw [← flipTransform_toQDivisor, ← flipTransform_toQDivisor, map_add, map_add, hDr,
    Nat.cast_smul_eq_nsmul, map_nsmul, map_nsmul, map_nsmul, smul_add, natCast_zsmul,
    natCast_zsmul]

/-- **Kollár–Mori, Cor. 6.4(2).** For a `(K + D)`-flipping contraction `f : X ⟶ Y` and `r > 0`
with `rD = Dr` integral, a `(K + D)`-flip of `f` exists if and only if the divisorial algebra
`R(Y, f_*(rK + rD))` has finitely generated `Γ(Y, U)`-algebras of sections over every affine
open `U ⊆ Y`. -/
@[mmp "thm_km3c_flip_exists_iff_fg"]
public theorem exists_isFlip_iff_finiteType_divisorialAlgebraSections
    {k : Type u} [Field k] {X Y : Scheme.{u}}
    (sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) (sY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [CompactSpace X] [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    [IsNormal X] [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [IsNormal Y]
    (K : Divisor X) (D : QDivisor X) (f : X ⟶ Y) (hf : IsFlippingContraction sX sY K D f)
    (r : ℕ) (hr : 0 < r) (Dr : Divisor X) (hDr : Divisor.toQDivisor Dr = (r : ℚ) • D) :
    (∃ (X' : Scheme.{u}) (sX' : X' ⟶ Spec (.of k)) (_ : CompactSpace X')
        (_ : IsLocallyNoetherian X') (_ : IsNormal X') (fp : X' ⟶ Y),
        IsFlip sX sY sX' K D f fp) ↔
      ∀ U : Y.Opens, IsAffineOpen U →
        Algebra.FiniteType Γ(Y, U)
          (Divisor.divisorialAlgebraSections
            (RationalMap.transformDivisor f.toRationalMap (r • K + Dr)) U) := by
  have hY := hf.isNormalVariety_target
  haveI : IsIntegral Y := hY.1.toIsIntegral
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨X', sX', _, _, _, fp, h⟩ U hU
    obtain ⟨-, -, -, -, -, hamp⟩ := h.isSmallAmpleModel hr
      (by rw [hDr, natCast_zsmul, Nat.cast_smul_eq_nsmul])
    haveI : IsIntegral X' := h.isNormalVariety.1.toIsIntegral
    haveI : IsProper fp := h.isProper
    haveI : IsDominant fp := h.isBirationalMorphism.isDominant
    exact Divisor.finiteType_divisorialAlgebraSections_of_inverseTransformDivisor fp
      h.two_le_codimension _ hamp U hU
  · intro hR
    obtain ⟨Z, _, _, _, sZ, g, hZ, hgY, hproj, hbir, hcodim, hQC, hamp⟩ :=
      Divisor.exists_isSmallAmpleModel_of_finiteType_divisorialAlgebra hY
        (RationalMap.transformDivisor f.toRationalMap (r • K + Dr)) fun y => by
          obtain ⟨U, hU, hyU, -⟩ :=
            exists_isAffineOpen_mem_and_subset (show y ∈ (⊤ : Y.Opens) from trivial)
          exact ⟨U, hU, hyU, hR U hU⟩
    have hT := toQDivisor_flipTransform_eq f g K D r Dr hDr
    change (Divisor.toQDivisor (flipTransform f g (r • K + Dr))).IsQCartier at hQC
    change (Divisor.toQDivisor (flipTransform f g (r • K + Dr))).HasRelativelyAmpleMultiple g
      at hamp
    rw [hT] at hQC hamp
    exact ⟨Z, sZ, ‹_›, ‹_›, ‹_›, g, hf, hZ, hgY, hproj.isProper, hbir,
      isQCartier_of_natCast_smul hr hQC, hasRelativelyAmpleMultiple_of_natCast_smul hr hamp,
      hcodim⟩

section CommonModel

open MMP.Flips
open scoped WithZero

/-- A local ring of an integral scheme `Y` birational to `X` which, inside the function field, is
the valuation ring of a valuation of `k(X)` is a valuation ring. -/
private theorem valuationRing_stalk_of_forall_le_one_iff {X Y : Scheme.{u}}
    [IsIntegral X] [IsIntegral Y] (β : Y ⟶ X) (hβ : IsBirationalMorphism β)
    {Γ : Type*} [LinearOrderedCommGroupWithZero Γ] (v : Valuation X.functionField Γ) (q : Y)
    (hq : haveI : IsDominant β := hβ.isDominant
      ∀ g : X.functionField, v g ≤ 1 ↔
        ∃ a : Y.presheaf.stalk q, algebraMap _ Y.functionField a = functionFieldMap β g) :
    ValuationRing (Y.presheaf.stalk q) := by
  haveI : IsDominant β := hβ.isDominant
  let φ := RingEquiv.ofBijective (functionFieldMap β) hβ.functionFieldMap_bijective
  let w : Valuation Y.functionField Γ := v.comap φ.symm.toRingHom
  have hw : ∀ r, w r ≤ 1 ↔ ∃ a : Y.presheaf.stalk q, algebraMap _ Y.functionField a = r := by
    intro r
    have := hq (φ.symm r)
    rwa [show functionFieldMap β (φ.symm r) = φ (φ.symm r) from rfl,
      RingEquiv.apply_symm_apply] at this
  exact ValuationRing.of_integers w
    ⟨IsFractionRing.injective _ _, fun a => (hw _).2 ⟨a, rfl⟩, fun r hr => (hw r).1 hr⟩

/-- A morphism of integral schemes, locally of finite type and birational in the sense of
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsBirational`, is a birational morphism. -/
private theorem isBirationalMorphism_of_isBirational {X Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X]
    [IsIntegral Y] (f : X ⟶ Y) [LocallyOfFiniteType f] (hf : IsBirational f) :
    IsBirationalMorphism f := by
  haveI : Finite (irreducibleComponents X) := by
    rw [irreducibleComponents_eq_singleton]
    exact Set.finite_singleton _
  haveI : Finite (irreducibleComponents Y) := by
    rw [irreducibleComponents_eq_singleton]
    exact Set.finite_singleton _
  obtain ⟨U, V, hUV, hU, hV, hiso⟩ :=
    exists_dense_opens_isIso_resLE_of_isBirational f hf (Or.inl ⟨inferInstance, inferInstance⟩)
  exact isBirationalMorphism_of_isIso_resLE f U V hU.nonempty hV.nonempty hUV hiso

/-- An ideal of the sections over an affine open extends to an ideal sheaf: the kernel of the
closed subscheme `Spec (Γ(X, U) ⧸ J) ⟶ X`, i.e. the ideal sheaf of its scheme-theoretic closure. -/
private theorem exists_idealSheafData_ideal_eq {X : Scheme.{u}} [QuasiSeparatedSpace X]
    (U : X.affineOpens) (J : Ideal Γ(X, U)) : ∃ ℐ : X.IdealSheafData, ℐ.ideal U = J := by
  have hU : IsAffineOpen (U : X.Opens) := U.2
  let φ := CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk J)
  let π : Spec (.of (Γ(X, U) ⧸ J)) ⟶ X := Spec.map φ ≫ hU.fromSpec
  refine ⟨π.ker, ?_⟩
  rw [Scheme.Hom.ker_apply]
  ext a
  rw [RingHom.mem_ker]
  have hle : (⊤ : (Spec (.of (Γ(X, U) ⧸ J))).Opens) ≤ π ⁻¹ᵁ U := by
    intro y _
    change hU.fromSpec ((Spec.map φ) y) ∈ (U : X.Opens)
    exact hU.range_fromSpec.subset ⟨_, rfl⟩
  have hres : (π.app U).hom a = 0 ↔ (π.appLE U ⊤ hle).hom a = 0 := by
    have heq : (homOfLE hle) = eqToHom (top_le_iff.mp hle).symm := Subsingleton.elim _ _
    rw [Scheme.Hom.appLE, heq, CommRingCat.comp_apply]
    exact (map_eq_zero_iff _ (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso
      ((Spec (.of (Γ(X, U) ⧸ J))).presheaf.map (eqToHom (top_le_iff.mp hle).symm).op)).1).symm
  have hcomp : π.appLE U ⊤ hle = (Scheme.ΓSpecIso Γ(X, U)).inv ≫ (Spec.map φ).appTop := by
    rw [Scheme.Hom.comp_appLE, hU.fromSpec_app_self, Category.assoc]
    congr 1
  rw [hres, hcomp, CommRingCat.comp_apply]
  have hnat := congrArg (fun g => g.hom ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso Γ(X, U)).inv.hom a))
    (Scheme.ΓSpecIso_naturality φ)
  simp only [CommRingCat.comp_apply, Iso.inv_hom_id_apply] at hnat
  rw [← map_eq_zero_iff _ (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso
    (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of (Γ(X, U) ⧸ J))).hom).1]
  erw [hnat]
  rw [CommRingCat.comp_apply]
  erw [Iso.inv_hom_id_apply]
  exact Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem (I := J)

/-- A unit of a ring mapping into the valuation ring of `w` maps to an element of value `1`. -/
private theorem valuation_eq_one_of_isUnit {S L : Type*} [CommRing S] [Field L] {Γ : Type*}
    [LinearOrderedCommGroupWithZero Γ] (w : Valuation L Γ) (φ : S →+* L)
    (hφ : ∀ s, w (φ s) ≤ 1) {t : S} (ht : IsUnit t) : w (φ t) = 1 :=
  letI := φ.toAlgebra
  Valuation.Integers.one_of_isUnit' ht hφ

/-- Let `φ : S → L` land in the valuation ring of `w`, with `S` essentially of finite type over
`R`. If a subring `C` contains the images of `R` and of the generators of `S`, every `φ s` is a
fraction `c / t` with `c, t ∈ C` and `w t = 1`. -/
private theorem exists_mul_eq_of_essFiniteType {R S L : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] [Algebra.EssFiniteType R S] [Field L] {Γ : Type*}
    [LinearOrderedCommGroupWithZero Γ] (w : Valuation L Γ) (φ : S →+* L)
    (hφ : ∀ s, w (φ s) ≤ 1) (C : Subring L) (hR : ∀ r, φ (algebraMap R S r) ∈ C)
    (hσ : ∀ s ∈ Algebra.EssFiniteType.finset R S, φ s ∈ C) (s : S) :
    ∃ c ∈ C, ∃ t ∈ C, w t = 1 ∧ φ s * t = c := by
  have hcond := (Algebra.essFiniteType_cond_iff R S (Algebra.EssFiniteType.finset R S)).mp
    (Algebra.EssFiniteType.isLocalization R S)
  have hadj : ∀ y ∈ Algebra.adjoin R (Algebra.EssFiniteType.finset R S : Set S), φ y ∈ C := by
    intro y hy
    induction hy using Algebra.adjoin_induction with
    | mem x hx => exact hσ x hx
    | algebraMap r => exact hR r
    | add x y _ _ hx hy => rw [map_add]; exact C.add_mem hx hy
    | mul x y _ _ hx hy => rw [map_mul]; exact C.mul_mem hx hy
  obtain ⟨t, ht, htu, hst⟩ := hcond s
  exact ⟨φ (s * t), hadj _ hst, φ t, hadj _ ht, valuation_eq_one_of_isUnit w φ hφ htu,
    (map_mul φ s t).symm⟩

/-- If every element of `J` has value at most that of `h`, every element of `Jⁿ` has value at
most that of `hⁿ`. -/
private theorem valuation_le_pow_of_mem_pow {A L : Type*} [CommRing A] [Field L] {Γ : Type*}
    [LinearOrderedCommGroupWithZero Γ] (w : Valuation L Γ) (ι : A →+* L)
    (hA : ∀ a, w (ι a) ≤ 1) (J : Ideal A) (h : A) (hJ : ∀ y ∈ J, w (ι y) ≤ w (ι h)) :
    ∀ n : ℕ, ∀ y ∈ J ^ n, w (ι y) ≤ w (ι h) ^ n := by
  intro n
  induction n with
  | zero => intro y _; rw [pow_zero]; exact hA y
  | succ n ih =>
    intro y hy
    rw [pow_succ] at hy
    refine Submodule.mul_induction_on hy (fun a ha b hb => ?_) (fun a b ha hb => ?_)
    · rw [map_mul, map_mul, pow_succ]
      exact mul_le_mul' (ih a ha) (hJ b hb)
    · rw [map_add]
      exact (w.map_add _ _).trans (max_le ha hb)

/-- The local rings of a scheme locally of finite type over a field `k` are essentially of
finite type over `k`. -/
private theorem essFiniteType_stalkAlgebra {k : Type u} [Field k] {Y : Scheme.{u}}
    (sY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [LocallyOfFiniteType sY] (y : Y) :
    letI := stalkAlgebra sY y
    Algebra.EssFiniteType k (Y.presheaf.stalk y) := by
  letI := stalkAlgebra sY y
  have := (sY.base y).isPrime
  have h0 : (algebraMap k (Localization.AtPrime (sY.base y).asIdeal)).EssFiniteType := by
    rw [RingHom.essFiniteType_algebraMap]
    exact Algebra.EssFiniteType.of_isLocalization _ (sY.base y).asIdeal.primeCompl
  have hiso : (Spec.stalkIso (.of k) (sY.base y)).inv.hom.EssFiniteType :=
    (RingHom.FiniteType.of_surjective _
      (asIso (Spec.stalkIso (.of k) (sY.base y)).inv).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.surjective
      ).essFiniteType
  have h1 : ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫
      (Spec (.of k)).presheaf.germ ⊤ (sY.base y) (by simp)).hom.EssFiniteType := by
    have e := congrArg CommRingCat.Hom.hom
      (Spec.algebraMap_stalkIso_inv (R := .of k) (x := sY.base y))
    rw [CommRingCat.hom_comp, CommRingCat.hom_ofHom] at e
    rw [← e]
    exact h0.comp hiso
  have h2 := h1.comp (LocallyOfFiniteType.stalkMap sY y)
  rw [← RingHom.essFiniteType_algebraMap]
  convert h2 using 1
  change ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ sY.appTop ≫ Y.presheaf.germ ⊤ y (by simp)).hom = _
  rw [← CommRingCat.hom_comp, Category.assoc, Scheme.Hom.germ_stalkMap]
  rfl

/-- Sections pulled back along a dominant morphism of integral schemes map to the function field
through `functionFieldMap`. -/
private theorem germToFunctionField_appLE {X Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X] [IsIntegral Y]
    (f : Y ⟶ X) [IsDominant f] (U : X.Opens) (V : Y.Opens) [Nonempty U] [Nonempty V]
    (h : V ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ U) (s : Γ(X, U)) :
    Y.germToFunctionField V (f.appLE U V h s) = functionFieldMap f (X.germToFunctionField U s) := by
  obtain ⟨⟨y, hy⟩⟩ := ‹Nonempty V›
  rw [← Scheme.algebraMap_germ_eq_germToFunctionField (X := Y) hy,
    ← Scheme.algebraMap_germ_eq_germToFunctionField (X := X) (h hy),
    MMP.Mori.functionFieldMap_algebraMap_stalk]
  congr 1
  erw [Scheme.Hom.germ_stalkMap_apply]
  rw [Scheme.Hom.appLE, CommRingCat.comp_apply, TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply]

/-- The constants `k ⊆ k(X)` are sections over every nonempty open. -/
private theorem exists_germToFunctionField_eq_algebraMap {k : Type u} [Field k] {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsIntegral X] (U : X.Opens) [Nonempty U] (c : k) :
    letI := functionFieldAlgebra sX
    ∃ a : Γ(X, U), X.germToFunctionField U a = algebraMap k X.functionField c := by
  letI := functionFieldAlgebra sX
  refine ⟨X.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op (sX.appTop ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv c)), ?_⟩
  change X.presheaf.germ U _ _ _ = ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ sX.appTop ≫
    X.presheaf.germ ⊤ (genericPoint X) (by simp)) c
  rw [TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply]
  rfl

/-- If a valuation `w` is at most `1` on the image of `ψ : T →+* L`, the elements of `T` whose
image has value `< 1` form a prime ideal. -/
private theorem exists_isPrime_valuation_lt_one {T L Γ : Type*} [CommRing T] [Field L]
    [LinearOrderedCommGroupWithZero Γ] (w : Valuation L Γ) (ψ : T →+* L)
    (hle : ∀ t, w (ψ t) ≤ 1) : ∃ 𝔮 : Ideal T, 𝔮.IsPrime ∧ ∀ t, t ∈ 𝔮 ↔ w (ψ t) < 1 := by
  let 𝔮 : Ideal T :=
    { carrier := {t | w (ψ t) < 1}
      add_mem' := fun {y z} hy hz => by
        simp only [Set.mem_setOf_eq, map_add] at *
        exact (w.map_add _ _).trans_lt (max_lt hy hz)
      zero_mem' := by simp
      smul_mem' := fun c y hy => by
        simp only [Set.mem_setOf_eq, smul_eq_mul, map_mul] at *
        exact (mul_le_of_le_one_left' (hle c)).trans_lt hy }
  have h𝔮 : ∀ t, t ∈ 𝔮 ↔ w (ψ t) < 1 := fun _ => Iff.rfl
  refine ⟨𝔮, ⟨?_, fun {y z} h => ?_⟩, h𝔮⟩
  · rw [Ideal.ne_top_iff_one, h𝔮, map_one, map_one]
    exact lt_irrefl _
  · rw [h𝔮, map_mul, map_mul] at h
    rw [h𝔮, h𝔮]
    by_contra hc
    push Not at hc
    rw [le_antisymm (hle y) hc.1, le_antisymm (hle z) hc.2, one_mul] at h
    exact lt_irrefl _ h

/-- In a localization `A = T_P` mapping to `L`, where `P` is the locus of `w ∘ ψ < 1`, every
`ψ c / ψ t` with `w (ψ t) = 1` comes from `A`. -/
private theorem exists_algebraMap_mul_eq_of_isLocalization {T A L Γ : Type*} [CommRing T]
    [CommRing A] [Field L] [LinearOrderedCommGroupWithZero Γ] (w : Valuation L Γ) (ψ : T →+* L)
    (P : Ideal T) [P.IsPrime] [Algebra T A] [IsLocalization P.primeCompl A] [Algebra A L]
    (hμ : ∀ t, algebraMap A L (algebraMap T A t) = ψ t) (hP : ∀ t, t ∈ P ↔ w (ψ t) < 1)
    (c t : T) (ht : w (ψ t) = 1) : ∃ a : A, algebraMap A L a * ψ t = ψ c := by
  have htq : t ∈ P.primeCompl := fun h => ((hP t).1 h).ne ht
  refine ⟨IsLocalization.mk' A c ⟨t, htq⟩, ?_⟩
  rw [← hμ, ← hμ, ← map_mul]
  exact congrArg _ (IsLocalization.mk'_spec A c ⟨t, htq⟩)

/-- In a localization `A = T_P` mapping to `L`, where `P` is the locus of `w ∘ ψ < 1` and
`w ∘ ψ ≤ 1`, the valuation `w` is at most `1` on `A`. -/
private theorem valuation_algebraMap_le_one_of_isLocalization {T A L Γ : Type*} [CommRing T]
    [CommRing A] [Field L] [LinearOrderedCommGroupWithZero Γ] (w : Valuation L Γ) (ψ : T →+* L)
    (hle : ∀ t, w (ψ t) ≤ 1) (P : Ideal T) [P.IsPrime] [Algebra T A]
    [IsLocalization P.primeCompl A] [Algebra A L]
    (hμ : ∀ t, algebraMap A L (algebraMap T A t) = ψ t) (hP : ∀ t, t ∈ P ↔ w (ψ t) < 1)
    (y : A) : w (algebraMap A L y) ≤ 1 := by
  obtain ⟨⟨c, t⟩, rfl⟩ := IsLocalization.mk'_surjective P.primeCompl y
  have ht1 : w (ψ t) = 1 := le_antisymm (hle t) (not_lt.mp (mt (hP t).2 t.2))
  have hmk : algebraMap A L (IsLocalization.mk' A c t) * ψ t = ψ c := by
    rw [← hμ, ← hμ, ← map_mul, IsLocalization.mk'_spec]
  calc w (algebraMap A L (IsLocalization.mk' A c t))
      = w (algebraMap A L (IsLocalization.mk' A c t)) * w (ψ t) := by rw [ht1, mul_one]
    _ = w (ψ c) := by rw [← map_mul, hmk]
    _ ≤ 1 := hle c

/-- In a localization `A = T_P` mapping to `L`, where `P` is the locus of `w ∘ ψ < 1`, every
element of an essentially finite type algebra mapped into `L` with value `≤ 1`, whose generators
land in the image of `ψ`, comes from `A`. -/
private theorem exists_algebraMap_eq_of_essFiniteType_of_isLocalization {R S T A L Γ : Type*}
    [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] [Algebra.EssFiniteType R S] [CommRing T] [CommRing A]
    [Field L] [LinearOrderedCommGroupWithZero Γ] (w : Valuation L Γ) (φ : S →+* L)
    (hφ : ∀ s, w (φ s) ≤ 1) (ψ : T →+* L) (hR : ∀ r, φ (algebraMap R S r) ∈ ψ.range)
    (hσ : ∀ s ∈ Algebra.EssFiniteType.finset R S, φ s ∈ ψ.range) (P : Ideal T) [P.IsPrime]
    [Algebra T A] [IsLocalization P.primeCompl A] [Algebra A L]
    (hμ : ∀ t, algebraMap A L (algebraMap T A t) = ψ t) (hP : ∀ t, t ∈ P ↔ w (ψ t) < 1)
    (s : S) : ∃ a : A, algebraMap A L a = φ s := by
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨c, rfl⟩, _, ⟨t, rfl⟩, ht, hct⟩ :=
    exists_mul_eq_of_essFiniteType w φ hφ ψ.range hR hσ s
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := exists_algebraMap_mul_eq_of_isLocalization w ψ P hμ hP c t ht
  have hψt : ψ t ≠ 0 := fun h => by
    rw [h, map_zero] at ht
    exact zero_ne_one ht
  exact ⟨y, mul_right_cancel₀ hψt (hy.trans hct.symm)⟩

/-- In a localization `A = T_P` mapping to `L`, where `P` is the locus of `w ∘ ψ < 1` and
`w ∘ fβ = v`, the valuation ring of `v`, the range of an essentially finite type algebra whose
generators land in the image of `ψ`, is the preimage under `fβ` of the image of `A`. -/
private theorem valuation_le_one_iff_exists_algebraMap_eq {R S T A K L Γ : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] [Algebra.EssFiniteType R S] [CommRing T] [CommRing A] [Field K]
    [Field L] [LinearOrderedCommGroupWithZero Γ] (v : Valuation K Γ) (w : Valuation L Γ)
    (fβ : K →+* L) (hw : ∀ g, w (fβ g) = v g) (φ : S →+* K) (hφ : ∀ g, v g ≤ 1 ↔ ∃ s, φ s = g)
    (ψ : T →+* L) (hTle : ∀ t, w (ψ t) ≤ 1) (hR : ∀ r, (fβ.comp φ) (algebraMap R S r) ∈ ψ.range)
    (hσ : ∀ s ∈ Algebra.EssFiniteType.finset R S, (fβ.comp φ) s ∈ ψ.range) (P : Ideal T)
    [P.IsPrime] [Algebra T A] [IsLocalization P.primeCompl A] [Algebra A L]
    (hμ : ∀ t, algebraMap A L (algebraMap T A t) = ψ t) (hP : ∀ t, t ∈ P ↔ w (ψ t) < 1)
    (g : K) : v g ≤ 1 ↔ ∃ a : A, algebraMap A L a = fβ g := by
  constructor
  · intro hg
    obtain ⟨s, rfl⟩ := (hφ g).1 hg
    exact exists_algebraMap_eq_of_essFiniteType_of_isLocalization w (fβ.comp φ)
      (fun s => by
        rw [RingHom.comp_apply, hw]
        exact (hφ _).2 ⟨s, rfl⟩) ψ hR hσ P hμ hP s
  · rintro ⟨y, hy⟩
    rw [← hw, ← hy]
    exact valuation_algebraMap_le_one_of_isLocalization w ψ hTle P hμ hP y

/-- If `t * χ h₀ ^ n = χ y` with `y ∈ J ^ n`, where `J` is bounded by `h₀` under `v ∘ ι`, then
`w (ψ t) ≤ 1`, for `w` pulling `v` back along `fβ` and `ψ ∘ χ = fβ ∘ ι`. -/
private theorem valuation_le_one_of_mul_pow_eq {R T K L Γ : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing T]
    [Field K] [Field L] [LinearOrderedCommGroupWithZero Γ] (v : Valuation K Γ)
    (w : Valuation L Γ) (ι : R →+* K) (χ : R →+* T) (ψ : T →+* L) (fβ : K →+* L)
    (hψχ : ∀ s, ψ (χ s) = fβ (ι s)) (hw : ∀ g, w (fβ g) = v g) (hιle : ∀ a, v (ι a) ≤ 1)
    (J : Ideal R) (h₀ : R) (hJ : ∀ y ∈ J, v (ι y) ≤ v (ι h₀)) (hh₀ : ι h₀ ≠ 0) {t : T} {n : ℕ}
    {y : R} (hy : y ∈ J ^ n) (hty : t * χ h₀ ^ n = χ y) : w (ψ t) ≤ 1 := by
  have h1 : ψ t * fβ (ι h₀) ^ n = fβ (ι y) := by
    simpa only [map_mul, map_pow, hψχ] using congrArg ψ hty
  have h2 : w (ψ t) * v (ι h₀) ^ n = v (ι y) := by
    rw [← hw, ← hw, ← map_pow, ← map_mul, h1]
  have h3 := valuation_le_pow_of_mem_pow v ι hιle J h₀ hJ n y hy
  rw [← h2] at h3
  exact (mul_le_iff_le_one_left (pow_pos (zero_lt_iff.mpr ((map_ne_zero v).mpr hh₀)) n)).mp h3

/-- If `w ∘ ι ≤ 1` and every element of `G` has value at most that of `h`, so does every
element of the ideal spanned by `h` and `G`. -/
private theorem valuation_le_of_mem_span_insert {A L Γ : Type*} [CommRing A] [Field L]
    [LinearOrderedCommGroupWithZero Γ] (w : Valuation L Γ) (ι : A →+* L)
    (hA : ∀ a, w (ι a) ≤ 1) (h : A) (G : Set A) (hG : ∀ z ∈ G, w (ι z) ≤ w (ι h)) :
    ∀ y ∈ Ideal.span (insert h G), w (ι y) ≤ w (ι h) := by
  intro y hy
  induction hy using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem z hz =>
    rcases hz with rfl | hz
    · exact le_rfl
    · exact hG z hz
  | zero => rw [map_zero, map_zero]; exact zero_le'
  | add y z _ _ hy hz => rw [map_add]; exact (w.map_add _ _).trans (max_le hy hz)
  | smul c y _ hy =>
    rw [smul_eq_mul, map_mul, map_mul]
    exact (mul_le_of_le_one_left' (hA c)).trans hy

/-- On the blow-up of an ideal sheaf restricting to `(h₀, g₁, …, gₖ)` on an affine open
`U ∋ x`, where the `gᵢ / h₀` generate the valuation ring of `v`, the point of the chart
`Spec Γ(X, U)[J/h₀]` cut out by `𝔪_v` lies over `x` and has the valuation ring of `v` as local
ring. -/
private theorem exists_blowUpChart_stalk_eq_integer {k : Type u} [Field k] {X : Scheme.{u}}
    [IsIntegral X] [Algebra k X.functionField] {v : Valuation X.functionField ℤᵐ⁰}
    {S : Type u} [CommRing S] [Algebra k S] [Algebra.EssFiniteType k S]
    (φ : S →ₐ[k] X.functionField) (hφ : ∀ g, v g ≤ 1 ↔ g ∈ φ.range) {x : X} (U : X.Opens)
    (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hxU : x ∈ U) [Nonempty U]
    (hk : ∀ r : k, ∃ c : Γ(X, U), X.germToFunctionField U c = algebraMap k X.functionField r)
    (hιle : ∀ a, v ((X.germToFunctionField U).hom a) ≤ 1)
    (hιlt : ∀ a, a ∈ (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩).asIdeal ↔ v ((X.germToFunctionField U).hom a) < 1)
    {h₀ : Γ(X, U)} (hh₀0 : h₀ ≠ 0) (g : S → Γ(X, U))
    (hg : ∀ s ∈ Algebra.EssFiniteType.finset k S,
      (X.germToFunctionField U).hom (g s) = (X.germToFunctionField U).hom h₀ * φ s)
    (ℐ : X.IdealSheafData)
    (hℐ : ℐ.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩ = Ideal.span (insert h₀ (g '' Algebra.EssFiniteType.finset k S)))
    [IsIntegral (blowUp ℐ)] [IsDominant (blowUpToBase ℐ)]
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (functionFieldMap (blowUpToBase ℐ))) :
    ∃ q : blowUp ℐ, blowUpToBase ℐ q = x ∧
      ∀ g : X.functionField, v g ≤ 1 ↔ ∃ a : (blowUp ℐ).presheaf.stalk q,
        algebraMap _ (blowUp ℐ).functionField a = functionFieldMap (blowUpToBase ℐ) g := by
  set ι : Γ(X, U) →+* X.functionField := (X.germToFunctionField U).hom
  have hιinj : Function.Injective ι := X.germToFunctionField_injective U
  set σ := Algebra.EssFiniteType.finset k S
  set J : Ideal Γ(X, U) := Ideal.span (insert h₀ (g '' σ))
  have hJ : ∀ y ∈ J, v (ι y) ≤ v (ι h₀) := valuation_le_of_mem_span_insert v ι hιle h₀ _ <| by
    rintro _ ⟨s, hs, rfl⟩
    rw [hg s hs, map_mul]
    exact mul_le_of_le_one_right' ((hφ _).2 ⟨s, rfl⟩)
  let U' : X.affineOpens := ⟨U, hU⟩
  have hmemJ : ∀ y ∈ J, y ∈ ℐ.ideal U' := fun y hy => by rw [hℐ]; exact hy
  let a : ℐ.ideal U' := ⟨h₀, hmemJ _ (Ideal.subset_span (Set.mem_insert _ _))⟩
  let W := blowUpChartOpen ℐ U' a
  have hW : IsAffineOpen W.1 := W.2
  have hWle : W.1 ≤ blowUpToBase ℐ ⁻¹ᵁ U := blowUpChartOpen_le ℐ U' a
  let χ : Γ(X, U) →+* Γ(blowUp ℐ, W.1) := (blowUpChartMap ℐ U' a).hom
  haveI : Nontrivial Γ(blowUp ℐ, W.1) := by
    haveI : Nontrivial (Localization.Away h₀) := ⟨⟨_, _, (IsLocalization.injective
      (Localization.Away h₀) (powers_le_nonZeroDivisors_of_noZeroDivisors hh₀0)).ne zero_ne_one⟩⟩
    exact (blowUpChartRingIso ℐ U' a).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.toEquiv.nontrivial
  have hmemW : ∀ p : Spec Γ(blowUp ℐ, W.1), hW.fromSpec p ∈ W.1 := fun p =>
    hW.range_fromSpec.subset ⟨p, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨p₀, hp₀⟩ := Ideal.exists_maximal Γ(blowUp ℐ, W.1)
  haveI : Nonempty W.1 :=
    ⟨⟨hW.fromSpec (show Spec _ from ⟨p₀, hp₀.isPrime⟩), hmemW _⟩⟩
  let ψ : Γ(blowUp ℐ, W.1) →+* (blowUp ℐ).functionField :=
    ((blowUp ℐ).germToFunctionField W.1).hom
  set fβ := functionFieldMap (blowUpToBase ℐ)
  have hψχ : ∀ s, ψ (χ s) = fβ (ι s) := fun s =>
    germToFunctionField_appLE (blowUpToBase ℐ) U W.1 hWle s
  let e := RingEquiv.ofBijective fβ ⟨fβ.injective, hsurj⟩
  let w : Valuation (blowUp ℐ).functionField ℤᵐ⁰ := v.comap e.symm.toRingHom
  have hw : ∀ g, w (fβ g) = v g := fun g => by
    simp only [w, Valuation.comap_apply, RingEquiv.toRingHom_eq_coe, RingHom.coe_coe]
    exact congrArg v (e.symm_apply_apply g)
  have hfh₀ : fβ (ι h₀) ≠ 0 := by
    rw [map_ne_zero, ne_eq, ← map_zero ι]; exact fun h => hh₀0 (hιinj h)
  have hTle : ∀ t, w (ψ t) ≤ 1 := fun t => by
    obtain ⟨n, y, hy, hty⟩ := exists_mem_pow_mul_eq_blowUpChartMap ℐ U' a t
    exact valuation_le_one_of_mul_pow_eq v w ι χ ψ fβ hψχ hw hιle J h₀ hJ
      (fun h => hh₀0 (hιinj (h.trans (map_zero ι).symm))) (hℐ ▸ hy) hty
  have hR : ∀ r, (fβ.comp φ.toRingHom) (algebraMap k S r) ∈ ψ.range := by
    intro r
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hk r
    refine ⟨χ c, ?_⟩
    rw [hψχ]
    change fβ (ι c) = fβ (φ (algebraMap k S r))
    rw [φ.commutes]
    exact congrArg fβ hc
  have hσ : ∀ s ∈ σ, (fβ.comp φ.toRingHom) s ∈ ψ.range := by
    intro s hs
    have hgs : g s ∈ ℐ.ideal U' :=
      hmemJ _ (Ideal.subset_span (Set.mem_insert_of_mem _ ⟨s, hs, rfl⟩))
    obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := exists_mul_eq_blowUpChartMap_of_mem_pow ℐ U' a (n := 1) (x := g s)
      (by rw [pow_one]; exact hgs)
    refine ⟨t, ?_⟩
    have ht' : χ (g s) = χ h₀ ^ 1 * t := ht
    have := congrArg ψ ht'
    rw [pow_one, map_mul, hψχ, hψχ, hg s hs, map_mul] at this
    exact (mul_left_cancel₀ hfh₀ this).symm
  obtain ⟨𝔮, h𝔮p, h𝔮⟩ := exists_isPrime_valuation_lt_one w ψ hTle
  let P : PrimeSpectrum Γ(blowUp ℐ, W.1) := ⟨𝔮, h𝔮p⟩
  have hqW : hW.fromSpec P ∈ W.1 := hmemW P
  have hPq := hW.primeIdealOf_fromSpec P hqW
  refine ⟨hW.fromSpec P, ?_, ?_⟩
  · have h1 := IsAffineOpen.comap_primeIdealOf_appLE (f := blowUpToBase ℐ) U hU W.1 hW hWle hqW
    have h2 : hU.primeIdealOf ⟨blowUpToBase ℐ (hW.fromSpec P), hWle hqW⟩ =
        hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩ := by
      rw [← h1, hPq]
      apply PrimeSpectrum.ext
      ext s
      rw [hιlt]
      change χ s ∈ 𝔮 ↔ _
      rw [h𝔮, hψχ, hw]
    have := congrArg hU.fromSpec h2
    rwa [hU.fromSpec_primeIdealOf, hU.fromSpec_primeIdealOf] at this
  · letI : Algebra Γ(blowUp ℐ, W.1) ((blowUp ℐ).presheaf.stalk (hW.fromSpec P)) :=
      TopCat.Presheaf.algebra_section_stalk _ ⟨_, hqW⟩
    haveI : IsLocalization P.asIdeal.primeCompl ((blowUp ℐ).presheaf.stalk (hW.fromSpec P)) :=
      hW.isLocalization_stalk' P hqW
    haveI := functionField_isScalarTower (blowUp ℐ) W.1 ⟨_, hqW⟩
    have hμ : ∀ t, algebraMap _ (blowUp ℐ).functionField (algebraMap Γ(blowUp ℐ, W.1)
        ((blowUp ℐ).presheaf.stalk (hW.fromSpec P)) t) = ψ t := fun t => by
      rw [← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply]; rfl
    exact valuation_le_one_iff_exists_algebraMap_eq v w fβ hw φ.toRingHom
      (fun g => (hφ g).trans (AlgHom.mem_range φ)) ψ hTle hR hσ P.asIdeal hμ h𝔮

/-- **The chart of the blow-up.** There are an affine open `U ∋ x` and a nonzero ideal
`J = (h₀, g₁, …, gₖ)` of `Γ(X, U)` such that, on the blow-up of any ideal sheaf restricting to `J`
on `U`, the point of the chart `Spec Γ(X, U)[J/h₀]` cut out by `𝔪_v` lies over `x` and has the
valuation ring of `v` as local ring. -/
private theorem exists_affineOpen_ideal_blowUp_stalk_eq_integer {k : Type u} [Field k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety k sX]
    {v : Valuation X.functionField ℤᵐ⁰}
    (hv : letI := functionFieldAlgebra sX
      ∃ (S : Type u) (_ : CommRing S) (_ : Algebra k S) (_ : Algebra.EssFiniteType k S)
        (φ : S →ₐ[k] X.functionField), ∀ g, v g ≤ 1 ↔ g ∈ φ.range) (x : X)
    (hle : ∀ a : X.presheaf.stalk x, v (algebraMap _ X.functionField a) ≤ 1)
    (hlt : ∀ a ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x),
      v (algebraMap _ X.functionField a) < 1) :
    ∃ (U : X.affineOpens) (J : Ideal Γ(X, U)), x ∈ (U : X.Opens) ∧ J ≠ ⊥ ∧
      ∀ (ℐ : X.IdealSheafData), ℐ.ideal U = J → ∀ [IsIntegral (blowUp ℐ)]
        [IsDominant (blowUpToBase ℐ)], Function.Surjective (functionFieldMap (blowUpToBase ℐ)) →
        ∃ q : blowUp ℐ, blowUpToBase ℐ q = x ∧
          ∀ g : X.functionField, v g ≤ 1 ↔ ∃ a : (blowUp ℐ).presheaf.stalk q,
            algebraMap _ (blowUp ℐ).functionField a = functionFieldMap (blowUpToBase ℐ) g := by
  haveI : IsIntegral X := ‹AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety k sX›.toIsIntegral
  letI := functionFieldAlgebra sX
  obtain ⟨S, _, _, _, φ, hφ⟩ := hv
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hxU, -⟩ :=
    exists_isAffineOpen_mem_and_subset (show x ∈ (⊤ : X.Opens) from trivial)
  haveI : Nonempty U := ⟨⟨x, hxU⟩⟩
  haveI := functionField_isFractionRing_of_isAffineOpen X U hU
  let ι : Γ(X, U) →+* X.functionField := (X.germToFunctionField U).hom
  have hι : ∀ a, algebraMap Γ(X, U) X.functionField a = ι a := fun _ => rfl
  have hιle : ∀ a, v (ι a) ≤ 1 := fun a => by
    rw [← Scheme.algebraMap_germ_eq_germToFunctionField (X := X) hxU]; exact hle _
  have hιlt : ∀ a, a ∈ (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩).asIdeal ↔ v (ι a) < 1 := by
    intro a
    rw [hU.primeIdealOf_eq_map_closedPoint]
    change X.presheaf.germ U x hxU a ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal _ ↔ _
    rw [← Scheme.algebraMap_germ_eq_germToFunctionField (X := X) hxU]
    refine ⟨hlt _, fun h => ?_⟩
    by_contra hm
    exact h.ne (valuation_eq_one_of_isUnit v _ hle (of_not_not hm))
  classical
  set σ := Algebra.EssFiniteType.finset k S
  obtain ⟨⟨h₀, hh₀⟩, hden⟩ :=
    IsLocalization.exist_integer_multiples_of_finset (nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, U)) (σ.image φ)
  have hden' : ∀ s ∈ σ, ∃ r : Γ(X, U), ι r = ι h₀ * φ s := fun s hs => by
    obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := hden (φ s) (Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ hs)
    exact ⟨r, by rw [← hι, hr, Algebra.smul_def, hι]⟩
  choose! g hg using hden'
  have hh₀0 : h₀ ≠ 0 := nonZeroDivisors.ne_zero hh₀
  refine ⟨⟨U, hU⟩, Ideal.span (insert h₀ (g '' σ)), hxU, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [ne_eq, Ideal.span_eq_bot]
    push Not
    exact ⟨h₀, Set.mem_insert _ _, hh₀0⟩
  intro ℐ hℐ _ _ hsurj
  exact exists_blowUpChart_stalk_eq_integer φ hφ U hU hxU
    (exists_germToFunctionField_eq_algebraMap sX U) hιle hιlt hh₀0 g hg ℐ hℐ hsurj

/-- **The blow-up step.** There is a projective birational `β : X₂ ⟶ X` from a variety and a
point `q ↦ x` of `X₂` whose local ring, inside `k(X)`, is the valuation ring of `v`. -/
private theorem exists_blowUp_stalk_eq_integer {k : Type u} [Field k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety k sX]
    {v : Valuation X.functionField ℤᵐ⁰}
    (hv : letI := functionFieldAlgebra sX
      ∃ (S : Type u) (_ : CommRing S) (_ : Algebra k S) (_ : Algebra.EssFiniteType k S)
        (φ : S →ₐ[k] X.functionField), ∀ g, v g ≤ 1 ↔ g ∈ φ.range) (x : X)
    (hle : ∀ a : X.presheaf.stalk x, v (algebraMap _ X.functionField a) ≤ 1)
    (hlt : ∀ a ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x),
      v (algebraMap _ X.functionField a) < 1) :
    ∃ (X₂ : Scheme.{u}) (β : X₂ ⟶ X) (_ : AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety k (β ≫ sX))
      (hβ : IsBirationalMorphism β),
      IsProjective β ∧ ∃ q : X₂, β q = x ∧
        haveI : IsDominant β := hβ.isDominant
        ∀ g : X.functionField, v g ≤ 1 ↔
          ∃ a : X₂.presheaf.stalk q, algebraMap _ X₂.functionField a = functionFieldMap β g := by
  obtain ⟨U, J, -, hJ, hchart⟩ := exists_affineOpen_ideal_blowUp_stalk_eq_integer sX hv x hle hlt
  haveI : QuasiSeparatedSpace X := quasiSeparatedSpace_of_quasiSeparated sX
  obtain ⟨ℐ, hℐ⟩ := exists_idealSheafData_ideal_eq U J
  have hℐ0 : ℐ ≠ ⊥ := by
    rintro rfl
    exact hJ (hℐ.symm.trans rfl)
  obtain ⟨hvar, hproj, hbir⟩ :=
    MMP.Flips.ResolutionInputs.isVariety_blowUp_and_isProjective_and_isBirational sX ℐ hℐ0
  haveI : IsIntegral (blowUp ℐ) := hvar.toIsIntegral
  haveI : IsIntegral X := ‹AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety k sX›.toIsIntegral
  haveI : IsProper (blowUpToBase ℐ) := hproj.isProper
  have hβ := isBirationalMorphism_of_isBirational (blowUpToBase ℐ) hbir
  haveI : IsDominant (blowUpToBase ℐ) := hβ.isDominant
  obtain ⟨q, hq, hstalk⟩ := hchart ℐ hℐ hβ.functionFieldMap_bijective.2
  exact ⟨blowUp ℐ, blowUpToBase ℐ, hvar, hβ, hproj, q, hq, hstalk⟩

/-- **The normalization step.** The normalization of a variety is a finite, hence projective,
birational morphism from a normal variety, and it is an isomorphism on local rings over a point
whose local ring is a valuation ring. -/
private theorem exists_normalization_isIso_stalkMap {k : Type u} [Field k] {Y : Scheme.{u}}
    (sY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety k sY] (q : Y)
    [ValuationRing (Y.presheaf.stalk q)] :
    ∃ (Z : Scheme.{u}) (ν : Z ⟶ Y), IsNormalVariety k (ν ≫ sY) ∧ IsProjective ν ∧
      IsBirationalMorphism ν ∧ ∃ z : Z, ν z = q ∧ IsIso (ν.stalkMap z) := by
  let ν := normalizationOverField k sY
  have hX := finite_irreducibleComponents_of_locallyOfFiniteType k sY
  have hbir : IsBirational ν := Scheme.isBirational_normalization Y hX
  haveI : IsFinite ν := isFinite_normalizationOverField k sY
  haveI hvar : AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety k (ν ≫ sY) := isVariety_normalizationOverField k sY
  haveI : IsIntegral (normalizationSchemeOverField k sY) := hvar.toIsIntegral
  have hνb : IsBirationalMorphism ν := isBirationalMorphism_of_isBirational ν hbir
  haveI : IsDominant ν := hνb.isDominant
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := (Scheme.surjective_normalization Y hX).surj q
  refine ⟨_, ν, ⟨hvar, Scheme.isNormal_normalizationScheme Y hX⟩,
    Stacks.FiniteMorphismProjective.isProjective_of_isFinite ν, hνb, z, hz, ?_⟩
  subst hz
  exact MMP.Positivity.isIso_stalkMap_of_valuationRing ν hνb.functionFieldMap_bijective z

/-- A dominant morphism which is an open immersion on a dense open is birational. -/
private theorem isBirationalMorphism_of_isOpenImmersion {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y)
    [IsDominant f] (U : X.Opens) (hU : Dense (U : Set X)) [IsOpenImmersion (U.ι ≫ f)] :
    IsBirationalMorphism f := by
  have hd : Dense ((U.ι ≫ f).opensRange : Set Y) := by
    rw [Scheme.Hom.coe_opensRange, Scheme.Hom.comp_base, TopCat.coe_comp, Set.range_comp,
      Scheme.Opens.range_ι]
    exact f.denseRange.dense_image f.continuous hU
  let e : X.PartialIso Y :=
    { source := U
      dense_source := hU
      target := (U.ι ≫ f).opensRange
      dense_target := hd
      iso := (U.ι ≫ f).isoOpensRange }
  refine ⟨e, ?_⟩
  rw [Scheme.PartialIso.toRationalMap, Scheme.PartialMap.toRationalMap_eq_iff]
  refine ⟨U, hU, le_rfl, le_top, ?_⟩
  simp only [Scheme.PartialMap.restrict, Scheme.PartialIso.toPartialMap_hom,
    Scheme.Hom.toPartialMap_hom, e, Scheme.Hom.isoOpensRange_hom_ι]
  exact (Scheme.homOfLE_ι_assoc _ _ _).trans
    (by rw [Scheme.topIso_hom]; exact (Scheme.homOfLE_ι_assoc _ _ _).symm)

/-- A birational morphism is an open immersion on a dense open. -/
private theorem exists_isOpenImmersion_of_isBirationalMorphism {X Y : Scheme.{u}} {f : X ⟶ Y}
    (hf : IsBirationalMorphism f) :
    ∃ U : X.Opens, Dense (U : Set X) ∧ IsOpenImmersion (U.ι ≫ f) := by
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := hf
  rw [Scheme.PartialIso.toRationalMap, Scheme.PartialMap.toRationalMap_eq_iff] at he
  obtain ⟨W, hW, hWe, hWf, h⟩ := he
  simp only [Scheme.PartialMap.restrict_hom] at h
  have he' : IsOpenImmersion e.toPartialMap.hom := by
    change IsOpenImmersion (e.iso.hom ≫ e.target.ι)
    infer_instance
  refine ⟨W, hW, ?_⟩
  have : W.ι ≫ f = X.homOfLE hWf ≫ f.toPartialMap.hom := by
    change W.ι ≫ f = (X.homOfLE (le_top : W ≤ ⊤) ≫ X.topIso.hom) ≫ f
    simp only [Scheme.topIso_hom, Scheme.homOfLE_ι]
  rw [this, ← h]
  infer_instance

/-- A composite of birational morphisms out of an irreducible scheme is birational. -/
private theorem isBirationalMorphism_comp {X Y Z : Scheme.{u}} [IrreducibleSpace X]
    {f : X ⟶ Y} {g : Y ⟶ Z} (hf : IsBirationalMorphism f) (hg : IsBirationalMorphism g) :
    IsBirationalMorphism (f ≫ g) := by
  haveI := hf.isDominant
  haveI := hg.isDominant
  obtain ⟨U₁, hU₁, h₁⟩ := exists_isOpenImmersion_of_isBirationalMorphism hf
  obtain ⟨U₂, hU₂, h₂⟩ := exists_isOpenImmersion_of_isBirationalMorphism hg
  let U : X.Opens := U₁ ⊓ f ⁻¹ᵁ U₂
  have hne : (U : Set X).Nonempty := by
    obtain ⟨x₀⟩ := (IrreducibleSpace.isIrreducible_univ X).nonempty
    haveI : Nonempty Y := ⟨f x₀⟩
    have hd : Dense (f '' U₁) := f.denseRange.dense_image f.continuous hU₁
    obtain ⟨y, hy₂, x, hx₁, rfl⟩ := (hU₂.inter_of_isOpen_left hd U₂.2).nonempty
    exact ⟨x, hx₁, hy₂⟩
  have hU : Dense (U : Set X) := U.2.dense hne
  have hle : U ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ U₂ := inf_le_right
  have hle₁ : U ≤ U₁ := inf_le_left
  have hres : IsOpenImmersion (f.resLE U₂ U hle) := by
    have : f.resLE U₂ U hle ≫ U₂.ι = X.homOfLE hle₁ ≫ (U₁.ι ≫ f) := by
      rw [Scheme.Hom.resLE_comp_ι, ← Category.assoc, Scheme.homOfLE_ι]
    have : IsOpenImmersion (f.resLE U₂ U hle ≫ U₂.ι) := by rw [this]; infer_instance
    exact IsOpenImmersion.of_comp _ U₂.ι
  haveI : IsOpenImmersion (U.ι ≫ f ≫ g) := by
    rw [← Category.assoc, ← Scheme.Hom.resLE_comp_ι f hle, Category.assoc]
    infer_instance
  exact isBirationalMorphism_of_isOpenImmersion (f ≫ g) U hU

/-- Transport of "the local ring at `ν z` is a given subset of `k(X)`" along a morphism `ν`
which is an isomorphism on local rings at `z`. -/
private theorem forall_iff_exists_stalk_comp {X Y Z : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X] [IsIntegral Y]
    [IsIntegral Z] (ν : Z ⟶ Y) (β : Y ⟶ X) [IsDominant ν] [IsDominant β] [IsDominant (ν ≫ β)]
    (z : Z) [IsIso (ν.stalkMap z)] (S : Set X.functionField)
    (hq : ∀ g : X.functionField, g ∈ S ↔
      ∃ a : Y.presheaf.stalk (ν z), algebraMap _ Y.functionField a = functionFieldMap β g) :
    ∀ g : X.functionField, g ∈ S ↔
      ∃ a : Z.presheaf.stalk z, algebraMap _ Z.functionField a = functionFieldMap (ν ≫ β) g := by
  intro g
  rw [hq g]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨a, ha⟩
    refine ⟨(ν.stalkMap z).hom a, ?_⟩
    rw [← MMP.Mori.functionFieldMap_algebraMap_stalk, ha,
      MMP.Positivity.DivisorOver.functionFieldMap_functionFieldMap_apply]
  · rintro ⟨b, hb⟩
    refine ⟨(inv (ν.stalkMap z)).hom b, (functionFieldMap ν).injective ?_⟩
    rw [MMP.Mori.functionFieldMap_algebraMap_stalk,
      MMP.Positivity.DivisorOver.functionFieldMap_functionFieldMap_apply, ← hb]
    congr 1
    exact congrArg (fun φ => φ.hom b) (IsIso.inv_hom_id (ν.stalkMap z))

/-- Two equivalent `ℤᵐ⁰`-valued valuations of a field which both take the value `exp (-1)` are
equal. -/
private theorem eq_of_isEquiv_of_exp_neg_one {K : Type*} [Field K] {w₁ w₂ : Valuation K ℤᵐ⁰}
    (h : w₁.IsEquiv w₂) (h₁ : ∃ a, w₁ a = WithZero.exp (-1))
    (h₂ : ∃ a, w₂ a = WithZero.exp (-1)) : w₁ = w₂ := by
  obtain ⟨ϖ, hϖ⟩ := h₁
  obtain ⟨ϖ', hϖ'⟩ := h₂
  have hpow : ∀ (w : Valuation K ℤᵐ⁰) (c : ℤ), w ϖ = WithZero.exp c → ∀ n : ℤ,
      w (ϖ ^ n) = WithZero.exp (c * n) := by
    intro w c hc n
    rw [map_zpow₀, hc, ← WithZero.exp_zsmul, smul_eq_mul, mul_comm]
  have hw₂ϖ : w₂ ϖ ≠ 0 := by
    rw [ne_eq, ← h.eq_zero, hϖ]; exact WithZero.exp_ne_zero
  set a := WithZero.log (w₂ ϖ)
  have ha : w₂ ϖ = WithZero.exp a := (WithZero.exp_log hw₂ϖ).symm
  have hw₁ϖ' : w₁ ϖ' ≠ 0 := by
    rw [ne_eq, h.eq_zero, hϖ']; exact WithZero.exp_ne_zero
  set b := WithZero.log (w₁ ϖ')
  have hb : w₁ ϖ' = WithZero.exp b := (WithZero.exp_log hw₁ϖ').symm
  have hab : w₂ ϖ' = WithZero.exp (a * -b) := by
    rw [← hpow w₂ a ha]
    exact (h.eq_iff).mp (by rw [hb, hpow w₁ (-1) hϖ]; congr 1; ring)
  rw [hϖ', WithZero.exp_inj] at hab
  have ha0 : a < 0 := by
    have : w₂ ϖ < 1 := (Valuation.isEquiv_iff_val_lt_one.mp h).mp
      (by rw [hϖ, ← WithZero.exp_zero, WithZero.exp_lt_exp]; omega)
    rwa [ha, ← WithZero.exp_zero, WithZero.exp_lt_exp] at this
  have ha1 : a = -1 := by
    have : a * b = 1 := by linarith
    rcases Int.eq_one_or_neg_one_of_mul_eq_one' this with h | h <;> omega
  ext g
  by_cases hg : g = 0
  · simp [hg]
  have hg1 : w₁ g ≠ 0 := by simp [hg]
  set m := WithZero.log (w₁ g)
  have hm : w₁ g = WithZero.exp m := (WithZero.exp_log hg1).symm
  have : w₂ g = w₂ (ϖ ^ (-m)) :=
    (h.eq_iff).mp (by rw [hm, hpow w₁ (-1) hϖ]; congr 1; ring)
  rw [this, hpow w₂ a ha, hm, ha1]
  congr 1
  ring

/-- If the local ring of `Z` at `z` is, inside `k(X)`, the valuation ring of a valuation taking
the value `exp (-1)`, it is not a field. -/
private theorem not_isField_stalk_of_valuation_eq_exp_neg_one {X Z : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X]
    [IsIntegral Z] (h : Z ⟶ X) [IsDominant h] (v : Valuation X.functionField ℤᵐ⁰) (z : Z)
    (hz : ∀ g : X.functionField, v g ≤ 1 ↔
      ∃ a : Z.presheaf.stalk z, algebraMap _ Z.functionField a = functionFieldMap h g)
    {g₀ : X.functionField} (hg₀ : v g₀ = WithZero.exp (-1)) :
    ¬ IsField (Z.presheaf.stalk z) := by
  intro hF
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := (hz g₀).1 (by rw [hg₀, ← WithZero.exp_zero, WithZero.exp_le_exp]; omega)
  have ha0 : a ≠ 0 := by
    rintro rfl
    rw [map_zero, eq_comm, map_eq_zero, ← v.zero_iff, hg₀] at ha
    exact WithZero.exp_ne_zero ha
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := hF.mul_inv_cancel ha0
  have hb' : v g₀⁻¹ ≤ 1 := (hz _).2 ⟨b, by
    rw [map_inv₀, ← ha]
    exact eq_inv_of_mul_eq_one_right (by rw [← map_mul, hb, map_one])⟩
  rw [map_inv₀, hg₀, ← WithZero.exp_neg, neg_neg, ← WithZero.exp_zero, WithZero.exp_le_exp] at hb'
  omega

/-- **The assembly step.** On a normal locally noetherian integral scheme `Z` dominating `X`, a
point `z` whose local ring is, inside `k(X)`, the valuation ring of a divisor `v` of `k(X)`, is
the generic point of a prime divisor `F` with `ord_F = v`. -/
private theorem exists_primeDivisor_valuationOver_eq {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral X]
    {v : Valuation X.functionField ℤᵐ⁰}
    (hv₁ : ∃ g, v g = WithZero.exp (-1)) {Z : Scheme.{u}} [IsIntegral Z]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian Z] [IsNormal Z] (h : Z ⟶ X) (hh : IsBirationalMorphism h) (z : Z)
    (hz : haveI : IsDominant h := hh.isDominant
      ∀ g : X.functionField, v g ≤ 1 ↔
        ∃ a : Z.presheaf.stalk z, algebraMap _ Z.functionField a = functionFieldMap h g) :
    ∃ F : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Z, F.genericPoint = z ∧
      haveI : IsDominant h := hh.isDominant
      F.valuationOver h = v := by
  haveI : IsDominant h := hh.isDominant
  haveI := valuationRing_stalk_of_forall_le_one_iff h hh v z hz
  obtain ⟨g₀, hg₀⟩ := hv₁
  have hnf := not_isField_stalk_of_valuation_eq_exp_neg_one h v z hz hg₀
  haveI : IsDiscreteValuationRing (Z.presheaf.stalk z) :=
    ((IsDiscreteValuationRing.TFAE (Z.presheaf.stalk z) hnf).out 1 2).mpr ‹_›
  have hcoh : Order.coheight z = 1 := by
    have h1 := ringKrullDim_stalk_eq_coheight z
    rw [IsDiscreteValuationRing.ringKrullDim_eq_one] at h1
    exact_mod_cast h1.symm
  refine ⟨AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.ofCoheightOne z hcoh,
    AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.genericPoint_ofCoheightOne z hcoh, ?_⟩
  set F : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Z := AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.ofCoheightOne z hcoh
  have hF : F.genericPoint = z := AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.genericPoint_ofCoheightOne z hcoh
  have hrange : ∀ r : Z.functionField,
      r ∈ (algebraMap F.localRing Z.functionField).range ↔
        ∃ a : Z.presheaf.stalk z, algebraMap _ Z.functionField a = r := by
    intro r
    change (∃ a : Z.presheaf.stalk F.genericPoint, _) ↔ _
    clear_value F
    subst hF
    rfl
  apply eq_of_isEquiv_of_exp_neg_one
  · refine Valuation.isEquiv_iff_val_le_one.mpr fun {g} => ?_
    rw [PrimeDivisor.valuationOver_apply, PrimeDivisor.divisorialValuation_le_one_iff, hrange,
      hz g]
  · haveI := F.isDiscreteValuationRing_localRing
    obtain ⟨ϖ, hϖ⟩ := IsDiscreteValuationRing.exists_irreducible F.localRing
    obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := hh.functionFieldMap_bijective.2 (algebraMap F.localRing Z.functionField ϖ)
    refine ⟨g, ?_⟩
    rw [PrimeDivisor.valuationOver_apply, hg]
    exact F.divisorialValuation_algebraMap_of_irreducible hϖ
  · exact ⟨g₀, hg₀⟩

/-- A normalized discrete valuation `v` of `k(X)` whose valuation ring is essentially of finite
type over `k` and dominates `𝒪_{X,x}` is `ord_F` for a divisor `(Z, h, F)` over `X`, `h`
projective with `h(η_F) = x`. -/
private theorem exists_properDivisorOver_of_essFiniteType {k : Type u} [Field k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety k sX]
    {v : Valuation X.functionField ℤᵐ⁰}
    (hv : letI := functionFieldAlgebra sX
      ∃ (S : Type u) (_ : CommRing S) (_ : Algebra k S) (_ : Algebra.EssFiniteType k S)
        (φ : S →ₐ[k] X.functionField), ∀ g, v g ≤ 1 ↔ g ∈ φ.range)
    (hv₁ : ∃ g, v g = WithZero.exp (-1)) (x : X)
    (hle : ∀ a : X.presheaf.stalk x, v (algebraMap _ X.functionField a) ≤ 1)
    (hlt : ∀ a ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x),
      v (algebraMap _ X.functionField a) < 1) :
    ∃ D : ProperDivisorOver k sX, IsProjective D.f ∧ D.valuation = v ∧
      D.f D.E.genericPoint = x := by
  obtain ⟨X₂, β, hvar₂, hβ, hprojβ, q, hqx, hq⟩ :=
    exists_blowUp_stalk_eq_integer sX hv x hle hlt
  haveI : IsIntegral X₂ := hvar₂.toIsIntegral
  haveI : IsDominant β := hβ.isDominant
  obtain ⟨Z, ν, hZ, hprojν, hν, z, hzq, hiso⟩ :=
    haveI := valuationRing_stalk_of_forall_le_one_iff β hβ v q hq
    exists_normalization_isIso_stalkMap (β ≫ sX) q
  subst hzq
  haveI : IsIntegral Z := hZ.1.toIsIntegral
  have hh : IsBirationalMorphism (ν ≫ β) := isBirationalMorphism_comp hν hβ
  have hZ' : IsNormalVariety k ((ν ≫ β) ≫ sX) := by rwa [Category.assoc]
  haveI : IsNormal Z := hZ.2
  haveI : IsLocallyNoetherian Z :=
    haveI : LocallyOfFiniteType ((ν ≫ β) ≫ sX) := hZ'.1.toLocallyOfFiniteType
    LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian ((ν ≫ β) ≫ sX)
  haveI : IsDominant ν := hν.isDominant
  haveI : IsDominant (ν ≫ β) := hh.isDominant
  have hz := forall_iff_exists_stalk_comp ν β z {g | v g ≤ 1} hq
  obtain ⟨F, hFz, hFv⟩ := exists_primeDivisor_valuationOver_eq hv₁ (ν ≫ β) hh z hz
  haveI : CompactSpace X := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace sX
  haveI : QuasiSeparatedSpace X := quasiSeparatedSpace_of_quasiSeparated sX
  have hproj : IsProjective (ν ≫ β) := IsProjective.comp hprojν hprojβ
  refine ⟨⟨⟨Z, ν ≫ β, hZ', hh, F⟩, hproj.isProper⟩, hproj, hFv, ?_⟩
  change (ν ≫ β) F.genericPoint = x
  rw [hFz, Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, hqx]

/-- **A divisor over `X` appears on a proper birational normal model of a given one.** Let
`u : Z₀ ⟶ X` be a proper birational morphism of normal varieties and `D` a divisor over `X`.
Then there is a proper birational morphism `h : Z ⟶ Z₀` from a normal variety and a prime
divisor `P` of `Z` whose valuation, through `h ≫ u`, is that of `D`. -/
private theorem exists_isProper_primeDivisor_valuation_eq {k : Type u} [Field k]
    {X Z₀ : Scheme.{u}} {sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)} (hX : IsNormalVariety k sX)
    (u : Z₀ ⟶ X) [IsProper u] (hu : IsBirationalMorphism u)
    (hZ₀ : IsNormalVariety k (u ≫ sX)) (D : DivisorOver k sX) :
    haveI : IsIntegral X := hX.1.toIsIntegral
    ∃ (Z : Scheme.{u}) (h : Z ⟶ Z₀) (hZ : IsNormalVariety k ((h ≫ u) ≫ sX))
      (hb : IsBirationalMorphism (h ≫ u)), IsProper h ∧ IsBirationalMorphism h ∧
      ∃ P : MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor Z, (⟨Z, h ≫ u, hZ, hb, P⟩ : DivisorOver k sX).valuation =
        D.valuation := by
  haveI : IsIntegral X := hX.1.toIsIntegral
  haveI : IsIntegral Z₀ := hZ₀.1.toIsIntegral
  haveI : IsDominant u := hu.isDominant
  haveI : AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety k (u ≫ sX) := hZ₀.1
  haveI := D.isIntegral
  haveI := D.isNormal
  haveI := D.isLocallyNoetherian
  haveI := D.isDominant
  letI := functionFieldAlgebra sX
  letI := functionFieldAlgebra (u ≫ sX)
  letI := functionFieldAlgebra (D.f ≫ sX)
  let Eu := functionFieldAlgEquiv sX u hu.functionFieldMap_bijective
  let ED := functionFieldAlgEquiv sX D.f D.isBirationalMorphism.functionFieldMap_bijective
  let v : Valuation Z₀.functionField (WithZero (Multiplicative ℤ)) :=
    D.valuation.comap (Eu.symm.toRingEquiv.toRingHom : Z₀.functionField →+* X.functionField)
  have hv : ∀ g, v g = D.E.divisorialValuation (ED (Eu.symm g)) := fun _ => rfl
  have hvu : ∀ g, v (functionFieldMap u g) = D.valuation g := fun g =>
    show D.valuation (Eu.symm (Eu g)) = _ by rw [AlgEquiv.symm_apply_apply]
  obtain ⟨x, ⟨hle, hlt⟩, -⟩ := (MMP.existsUnique_center_of_isProper hZ₀.1 hX.1 u rfl).2 hu D
  have hle' : ∀ a : Z₀.presheaf.stalk x, v (algebraMap _ Z₀.functionField a) ≤ 1 := fun a =>
    hle a _ (Eu.apply_symm_apply _)
  have hlt' : ∀ a ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Z₀.presheaf.stalk x),
      v (algebraMap _ Z₀.functionField a) < 1 := fun a ha =>
    hlt a ha _ (Eu.apply_symm_apply _)
  have hv₁ : ∃ g, v g = WithZero.exp (-1) := by
    haveI := D.E.isDiscreteValuationRing_localRing
    obtain ⟨ϖ, hϖ⟩ := IsDiscreteValuationRing.exists_irreducible D.E.localRing
    refine ⟨Eu (ED.symm (algebraMap D.E.localRing D.Y.functionField ϖ)), ?_⟩
    rw [hv, AlgEquiv.symm_apply_apply, AlgEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
    exact D.E.divisorialValuation_algebraMap_of_irreducible hϖ
  have hS : ∃ (S : Type u) (_ : CommRing S) (_ : Algebra k S) (_ : Algebra.EssFiniteType k S)
      (φ : S →ₐ[k] Z₀.functionField), ∀ g, v g ≤ 1 ↔ g ∈ φ.range := by
    haveI := D.isNormalVariety.1.toLocallyOfFiniteType
    letI := stalkAlgebra (D.f ≫ sX) D.E.genericPoint
    haveI := isScalarTower_stalk_functionField (D.f ≫ sX) D.E.genericPoint
    refine ⟨D.Y.presheaf.stalk D.E.genericPoint, inferInstance, inferInstance,
      essFiniteType_stalkAlgebra (D.f ≫ sX) D.E.genericPoint,
      Eu.toAlgHom.comp (ED.symm.toAlgHom.comp
        (IsScalarTower.toAlgHom k _ D.Y.functionField)), fun g => ?_⟩
    rw [hv, PrimeDivisor.divisorialValuation_le_one_iff]
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨a, ha⟩
      refine ⟨a, ?_⟩
      change Eu (ED.symm (algebraMap _ D.Y.functionField a)) = g
      rw [ha, AlgEquiv.symm_apply_apply, AlgEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
    · rintro ⟨a, rfl⟩
      refine ⟨a, ?_⟩
      change algebraMap _ D.Y.functionField a =
        ED (Eu.symm (Eu (ED.symm (algebraMap _ D.Y.functionField a))))
      rw [AlgEquiv.symm_apply_apply, AlgEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
  obtain ⟨D', -, hD'v, -⟩ := exists_properDivisorOver_of_essFiniteType (u ≫ sX) hS hv₁ x hle' hlt'
  haveI := D'.isIntegral
  haveI := D'.isDominant
  haveI := D'.isNormal
  haveI := D'.isLocallyNoetherian
  have hb : IsBirationalMorphism (D'.f ≫ u) := isBirationalMorphism_comp D'.isBirationalMorphism hu
  refine ⟨D'.Y, D'.f, by simpa only [Category.assoc] using D'.isNormalVariety, hb, D'.isProper,
    D'.isBirationalMorphism, D'.E, ?_⟩
  ext g
  rw [← hvu g, ← hD'v]
  show D'.E.divisorialValuation (functionFieldMap (D'.f ≫ u) g) =
    D'.E.divisorialValuation (functionFieldMap D'.f (functionFieldMap u g))
  rw [MMP.Positivity.DivisorOver.functionFieldMap_functionFieldMap_apply]

/-- In the situation of the common normal model
(`MMP.Mori.exists_isNormalVariety_isProper_isBirationalMorphism`), given a divisor `D` over `X₁`,
the model `Z` with `g₁ : Z ⟶ X₁`, `g₂ : Z ⟶ X₂` can be chosen so that moreover `D` appears on
`Z`: there is a prime divisor `P` of `Z` such that the divisor `(Z, g₁, P)` over `X₁` has the
valuation of `D`. -/
@[mmp "lem_km3c_common_model_with_divisor"]
public theorem exists_isNormalVariety_isProper_isBirationalMorphism_primeDivisor_valuation_eq
    {k : Type u} [Field k]
    {X₁ X₂ S : Scheme.{u}} {sX₁ : X₁ ⟶ Spec (.of k)} {sX₂ : X₂ ⟶ Spec (.of k)}
    (hX₁ : IsNormalVariety k sX₁) (hX₂ : IsNormalVariety k sX₂)
    (f₁ : X₁ ⟶ S) (f₂ : X₂ ⟶ S) [IsProper f₁] [IsProper f₂]
    (φ : RationalMap X₁ X₂) (hφ : φ.IsBirational) (hφS : φ.compHom f₂ = f₁.toRationalMap)
    (D : DivisorOver k sX₁) :
    haveI : IsIntegral X₁ := hX₁.1.toIsIntegral
    ∃ (Z : Scheme.{u}) (g₁ : Z ⟶ X₁) (g₂ : Z ⟶ X₂) (hZ : IsNormalVariety k (g₁ ≫ sX₁))
      (hg₁ : IsBirationalMorphism g₁),
      IsProper g₁ ∧ IsProper g₂ ∧ IsBirationalMorphism g₂ ∧
      (∃ φ' : X₁.PartialMap X₂, φ'.toRationalMap = φ ∧
        (g₁ ⁻¹ᵁ φ'.domain).ι ≫ g₂ = (g₁ ∣_ φ'.domain) ≫ φ'.hom) ∧
      g₁ ≫ f₁ = g₂ ≫ f₂ ∧
      ∃ P : PrimeDivisor Z,
        (⟨Z, g₁, hZ, hg₁, P⟩ : DivisorOver k sX₁).valuation = D.valuation := by
  obtain ⟨Z₀, u₁, u₂, hZ₀, hu₁p, hu₂p, hu₁, hu₂, ⟨φ', hφ', hrel⟩, hcomm⟩ :=
    exists_isNormalVariety_isProper_isBirationalMorphism hX₁ hX₂ f₁ f₂ φ hφ hφS
  obtain ⟨Z, h, hZ, hb, hhp, hh, P, hP⟩ :=
    exists_isProper_primeDivisor_valuation_eq hX₁ u₁ hu₁ hZ₀ D
  haveI : IsIntegral Z := hZ.1.toIsIntegral
  haveI : IsIntegral Z₀ := hZ₀.1.toIsIntegral
  haveI : IsIntegral X₂ := hX₂.1.toIsIntegral
  haveI : IsNormal Z₀ := hZ₀.2
  haveI : IsNormal X₂ := hX₂.2
  haveI := hZ₀.1.toLocallyOfFiniteType
  haveI := hX₂.1.toLocallyOfFiniteType
  haveI : IsLocallyNoetherian Z₀ := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian (u₁ ≫ sX₁)
  haveI : IsLocallyNoetherian X₂ := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian sX₂
  have hb₂ : IsBirationalMorphism (h ≫ u₂) := isBirationalMorphism_comp_of_isBirational u₂ h
    (MMP.Resolution.Bridges.isBirational_of_isBirationalMorphism hu₂)
    (MMP.Resolution.Bridges.isBirational_of_isBirationalMorphism hh)
  refine ⟨Z, h ≫ u₁, h ≫ u₂, hZ, hb, inferInstance, inferInstance, hb₂,
    ⟨φ', hφ', ?_⟩, by simp [hcomm], P, hP⟩
  have hres := morphismRestrict_comp h u₁ φ'.domain
  have e1 : ((h ≫ u₁) ∣_ φ'.domain) ≫ φ'.hom =
      (h ∣_ (u₁ ⁻¹ᵁ φ'.domain)) ≫ (u₁ ∣_ φ'.domain) ≫ φ'.hom := by
    rw [← Category.assoc]; exact congrArg (· ≫ φ'.hom) hres
  rw [e1, ← hrel, morphismRestrict_ι_assoc]
  rfl

end CommonModel

end MMP.Mori
